\par\par \b \uc2  WRAP:Thai Ctrl Bk Confirms  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  To Cap Baht's Rise \b0\par\par\uc2 587 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2003\par 11:24\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula Wednesday confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, buying dollars for baht to stem the sharp rise in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Sentiment for the baht, along with most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , has turned bullish recently due to broad dollar weakness amid doubts over the U.S. government's will to continue with its strong-dollar policy. \par \par \uc2  Large amounts of capital inflows from foreign investors parking money in local stocks has also added to the baht's recent rally, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to act in the market, Pridiyathorn said. \par \par \uc2  The baht has consistently been hitting fresh multi-month highs against the dollar over the past two weeks and traded a fresh 10-month high of 41.62 to the dollar intraday Wednesday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has strengthened around 3% versus the dollar since the beginning of the year. \par \par \uc2  At 0919 GMT, the dollar was trading at 41.67 baht, barely changed compared with THB41.68 at Tuesday's close in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The baht would be "unnaturally" strong if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Pridiyathorn told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "We are monitoring the market and will try to keep it (the baht) at an appropriate level. We did our best," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  However, he declined to say what amount of dollars the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought to cap the strength in the baht. \par \par \uc2  "The high foreign reserves and seven straight days' of gains in Thai stocks show you how much (foreign) money is flowing into Thailand," Pridiyathorn said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign net buying of Thai stocks so far this year has reached THB4.77 billion. Thai foreign reserves stood at $38.8 billion as of May 16, up from $38.4 billion a week earlier. \par \par \uc2  Traders said Pridiyathorn's remarks confirming the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  shouldn't have any significant impact on the baht as it's simply standard practice and therefore won't surprise. \par \par \uc2  "The market doesn't react to the comments as we all know that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has supported the dollar from time to time no matter if they say so or not," said a local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  The attractive value of Thai stocks vis-a-vis other nations in the region and the country's strong economic fundamentals are probably drawing in investors' money, Pridiyathorn said. \par \par \uc2  The strong baht also encourages demand in the bond market as most banks have sold dollars for baht. They have to channel that huge baht liquidity into the local bond market. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is monitoring any impact that the strong baht might have on Thai exports and imports, but noted Thailand's competitiveness compared with other Asian countries has remained unchanged in the last three to four years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has reiterated its managed-float policy many times. It has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market in a bid to help maintain \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's export competitiveness compared with other key rivals such as China. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn said he met with Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra Tuesday and briefed him on the capital inflows that had led to the baht's strength. \par \par \uc2  Thaksin said Tuesday he was pleased with the baht's current level, noting that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have been even stronger if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't been managing the exchange rate to keep it stable. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Simon Harvey \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030528dz5s000l5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
