\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Dn Late;Acctg Woes,N Korea Weigh On Won \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nirmala Menon \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 884 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2003\par 10:07\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The South Korean won recovered from a five-month intraday low to close just a touch weaker Thursday, but analysts said they expect more downside ahead stemming from a domestic accounting scandal and tensions from the communist North. \par \par \uc2  Most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  headed south as the dollar rose against major rivals and commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , such as the Australian dollar and the Canadian unit. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was lifted to a two-and-a-half week high against the yen in Asia on a spate of rumors and reports related to Iraq and North Korea. \par \par \uc2  Traders said there was no evidence of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region, though some suspected the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have been in the market to smooth out volatility in the dollar/baht. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's rise, coupled with increased concerns over North Korea's nuclear ambitions, "combined to put a better bid" on the U.S. unit across the region, said David Simmonds, senior emerging markets strategist at The Royal Bank of Scotland. \par \par \uc2  Concerns over the accounting scandal that erupted in South Korea earlier this week might have also had "a little bit of spillover" effect on the other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he added. \par \par \uc2  The won ended at a fresh five-month low of 1,245.6 to the dollar, slightly weaker from KRW1,245.0 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The won had earlier slipped to a five-month intraday low of KRW1,254.5, pressured by the accounting scandal at SK Global, the country's third largest conglomerate. South Korean prosecutors recently uncovered accounting irregularities worth KRW1.55 trillion at the company. \par \par \uc2  The won later recovered to peak at KRW1,237.0, after Moody's Investors Service affirmed the country's A3 sovereign rating; many market players had been expecting a downgrade. \par \par \uc2  But the rebound was short-lived as risk factors - the SK Global issue, the North's nuclear standoff with the U.S. and a weakening economy - returned to grip the market. \par \par \uc2  Increased South Korea risk has prompted some foreign banks in Seoul to reduce the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps they do with domestic banks, but this hasn't had much of an impact on the spot exchange rate, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "The foreign banks aren't absolutely going out of business with the local banks. They're just reducing their \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  swaps by a little amount," said a spot dealer. \par \par \uc2  "We still prefer to buy (dollars) on dips," said Frank Gong, Hong Kong-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Bank of America. "The trend for the won is weaker. There are many risks with the economy, corporate scandals and geopolitical tensions." \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht fell to as low as 42.83 to the dollar earlier in the session as offshore players bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is closely monitoring the baht's movements. \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's volatility was due to market rumors about developments in the war against terrorism. \par \par \uc2  "There was talk that Iraqi soldiers were surrendering and that (Osama) bin Laden got arrested. It's pretty messy here," a Bangkok-based trader said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is more sensitive to rumors these days. \par \par \uc2  Late in Asia, the baht was quoted at 42.72 to the dollar, from THB42.67 at the local close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar weakened but came off lows as some foreign banks took profits on the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Near the end of local trading hours, the U.S. unit was quoted at S$1.7494, up from S$1.7463 late Wednesday. The intraday trading range was between S$1.7470 and S$1.7540. \par \par \uc2  The New Taiwan dollar tracked the yen lower to end at its weakest level in eight sessions. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit ended at NT$34.739, up from Wednesday's NT$34.721, after trading between NT$34.735 and NT$34.819. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso snapped a three-day losing streak to close stronger for the first time this week as banks took profits on the dollar, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The peso finished at 54.950 to the dollar on the Philippine Dealing System, strengthening from Wednesday's record low of PHP55.099. \par \par \uc2  Some traders said the market was also rattled by talk late in the session that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was prepared to impose stricter \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rules to zero in on potential speculators. \par \par \uc2  After market close, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced a set of measures aimed at curbing speculation, including tighter monitoring of banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  deals and limiting their overbought dollar limit to 2.5% of capital. \par \par \uc2  Meantime, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Board left the closely watched overnight rates unchanged, citing a still benign inflation outlook. \par \par \uc2  But the board warned it may shift to a tightening bias if the weak peso threatens the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation target of 4.5%-5.5%. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah ended unchanged at 8,905 to the dollar, recovering from an intraday low of IDR8,925 on suspected dollar selling by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Nirmala Menon, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4046; nirmala.menon@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  -Edited by Bernice Tang \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030313dz3d000lu\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
