\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Higher On Early Offshore Dollar Selling \b0\par\par\uc2 687 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Februar 2003\par 11:39\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended higher against the dollar in Asian spot trade Tuesday after early selling in the U.S. unit by foreign players prompted talk that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  might have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  indirectly to stem the baht's slide, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 42.75 baht, down from THB42.83 at the Asian close Monday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar hit its intraday high of THB42.80 in the morning, but later gave up those gains on dollar selling by offshore European banks. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the dollar selling for baht prompted talk that European banks might have been acting on behalf of the Bank of Thailand to prevent the baht's depreciation, given the unusually heavy bids. \par \par \uc2  "But I don't think their demand for the baht has anything to do with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as the Finance Ministry has said the recent exchange rate is satisfactory," a Bangkok trader added. \par \par \uc2  "It's more likely that those banks wanted to transfer funds to local companies," he said. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said Monday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been monitoring the baht's movements in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to ensure that Thai export prices remain competitive. \par \par \uc2  Somkid said the baht's weakness in recent sessions has been in line with weakness in the yen, and the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  remains at a satisfactory level against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Thailand's regional trading partners. \par \par \uc2  The dollar fell to its intraday low of THB42.73 in the afternoon, before recovering slightly by the close. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to open Wednesday in a range of THB42.70-THB42.85. \par \par \uc2  Thai long-term government bond prices fell slightly on profit-taking after sharp gains Tuesday, but strong results in an initial auction of THB5 billion worth of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  364-day bonds reactivated short-term bonds, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The yield on the long-term issue due November 2012 finished at 3.06%, up from a close of 3.05% Monday, the Thai Bond Dealing Center said in its daily report. \par \par \uc2  But the curve steepened slightly, after flattening in most sessions since the beginning of the year, on buying in the short-end sparked by results of the auction, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auctioned its new bonds at an average yield of 1.54735%, further below the government bond yield curve than had been expected due to high financial system liquidity and prospects for an extended period of low interest rates. The government bond curve was at 1.57% at one year as of early Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Buying in the short-end of the curve pushed the yield on the government bond due June 2004 down to end at 1.585% from a previous close of 1.60%, the bond dealing center said. \par \par \uc2  A money market dealer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 14-day repurchase market target rate of 1.75% was out of line, too high for both money market interest rates and the treasury bill government bond yield curve. \par \par \uc2  But dealers aren't certain whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will cut the 14-day target, as it could lead to further declines in money market rates and commercial bank deposit account rates, which might attract unwanted political attention. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Monetary Policy Committee next meets March 3. The committee is expected to cut the 14-day target rate only if U.S. interest rates fall further, or if Iraq-related disruptions in the global oil, trade and tourism markets begins to hurt the Thai economy. \par \par \uc2  Overnight money market interest rates continued to fall as liquidity prepared for public demand over the unofficial Lunar New Year holidays returned to the system, with additional downward pressure from short-term debt market yields. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term            Tuesday          Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Late  1.50000%         1.53125%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close 1.43750%         1.50000%\par            14-Day          1.75000%         1.75000%\par            1-Month         no activity      1.75000%\par            3-Month         no activity      no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Rattaphol Onsanit and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744;\par djn.bangkok@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030204dz24000mf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
