\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: Demand-Supply Moves Baht; No Action Needed \b0\par\par\uc2 205 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2003\par 06:51\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Friday that no \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was necessary in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets as the baht was moving in line with demand and supply. \par \par \uc2  "Now we don't have to do anything. The baht is moving in line with demand and supply. Normally, if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying dollars I would get a report, but I haven't received anything so far today," Pridiyathorn said. \par \par \uc2  Reporters noted that investors, in recent weeks, have been reluctant to bet the baht would continue to strengthen because they were afraid the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would step in to buy dollars. \par \par \uc2  "It's good that there is no speculation," Pridiyathorn told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand has a policy of buying dollars on weakness to build foreign reserves and damp volatility. \par \par \uc2  Over the past few weeks, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has weakened against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the region. \par \par \uc2  At 0553 GMT Friday, the dollar was quoted at 42.835 baht, up from THB42.675 at the open, in line with a pullback in the yen against the U.S. unit. \par \par \uc2  -By Dow Jones Newswires Bangkok Bureau; 662 266 0744; djn.bangkok@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030117dz1h000a6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
