\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -SGD hits 6-month high, others ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 546 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Januar 2003\par 04:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE, Jan 17 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit\par fresh six-month highs early on Friday but other Asian\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were down as sentiment diverged on uncertainty over\par the near-term direction of the dollar/yen.\par     Dealers said the euro's climb to a three-year high against\par the dollar was enough to provide room for a stronger Singapore\par dollar, despite uncertainty over the yen's near-term direction.\par     Singapore authorities manage the exchange rate against an\par undisclosed trade-weighted basket of its major trading partners\par and most analysts believe yen and euro are major components of\par that basket.\par     The Singapore unit firmed to around 1.7294 per U.S. dollar,\par its strongest since July 22, when it saw a seven-month high of\par 1.7289.\par  \par     Dealers said players in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were bearish on\par the dollar in the near term.\par     But given the potential threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by Japan and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  by their own central banks to cap recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains, most \par \par \uc2  players were reluctant to extend their short dollar positions \par \par \uc2  over the weekend, they added. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar will continue to face selling pressure as long as \par \par \uc2  war jitters are around," said Lee Boon Keng, treasury markets \par \par \uc2  strategist at DBS Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "But should the war start, it will remove the biggest \par \par \uc2  source of uncertainty plaguing the market," he added, saying \par \par \uc2  players should be cautious. \par \par \uc2  Hit by intensifying tensions over the prospect of a war \par \par \uc2  against Iraq, the U.S. dollar eased beyond $1.06 against the \par \par \uc2  euro. \par \par \uc2  But it bounced off fresh three-year lows hit overnight \par \par \uc2  against the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and was supported against the yen \par \par \uc2  amid fears of Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to aid the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Japan's top financial diplomat, Zembei Mizoguchi, said the \par \par \uc2  finance ministry was always prepared to act as needed and was \par \par \uc2  watching \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves closely. \par \par \uc2  C.BANK WARINESS WEIGH ON BAHT \par \par \uc2  Elsewhere, the Thai baht was down to around 42.70 per \par \par \uc2  dollar, from early offshore highs at 42.63 but not far from \par \par \uc2  late Thursday's 42.68. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Singapore said overall sentiment was bullish on \par \par \uc2  the baht but players were wary of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to protect export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said they suspected some foreign banks on behalf of \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had pulled the baht off four-month highs of \par \par \uc2  42.54 per dollar hit on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     They said most players believe the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may again\par buy U.S. dollars around 42.50 to cap the baht's upside.\par     "With the weekend approaching and with all the uncertainty,\par players are covering their short dollar positions," said an\par offshore baht dealer at a European bank in Singapore.\par     The Philippines peso edged down to 53.55 per dollar, from\par Thursday's onshore close of 53.47, in thin trade.\par     Dealers in Manila said some downside peso support was\par spotted at around 53.50 as players covered short peso\par positions.\par     The Indonesian rupiah stayed supported within its recent\par 8,860-8,880 range as dollar demand from local corporates\par spotted through this week waned.\par     The Taiwan dollar touched a fresh two-month high before\par giving up those gains.\par     The South Korean won stepped back from early highs, amid\par caution over moves in the dollar/yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030117dz1h005k6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
