\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Soft dlr helps, rupiah heads for 4-month high. \b0\par\par\uc2 918 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2002\par 10:14\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     By Ovais Subhani\par     SINGAPORE, Dec 16 (Reuters) - The buoyant Indonesian\par rupiah\par  strengthened towards 8,800 per dollar on Monday, a break of\par which would take it to four-month peaks and far from the gloom\par that surrounded it after the devastating Bali attacks in\par October.\par     Most other Asian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also firmed against a broadly\par weaker dollar, the friendless Philippine peso the exception,\par with the Singapore dollar and Thai baht consolidating around\par their respective three-month and one-month highs.\par     The rupiah rose to around 8,805 per dollar, its highest\par since September 9, supported by Sunday's part sale of telco\par giant PT Indosat. Singapore's ST Telemedia will pay $634\par million for a 42 percent stake in the state-run telecom.\par     Dealers in Jakarta said while dollar demand from some local\par corporates capped the rupiah and thin conditions deterred\par aggressive moves, speculation over dollar inflows from the\par Indosat sale kept the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  supported.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Players are betting that at least 20 to 30 percent of the\par Indosat proceeds will flow into the market," said a dealer at\par an American bank in Jakarta.\par     He said that speculation could push the dollar beyond\par 8,800, and might have already halted some dollar purchases from\par corporates who can afford to wait for cheaper dollars.\par     The rupiah is Asia's best performing \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in 2002,\par rising over 17.6 percent against the dollar, backed by steady\par inflows from sale of state assets and repatriation of earnings\par from exports due to higher yields at home.\par     It has risen by almost seven percent from a six-month low\par around 9,400 per dollar reached after the October 12 bombings\par in Bali which killed almost 200 people, mostly foreign\par tourists.\par     SING, BAHT CONSOLIDATE\par     Elsewhere, dealers said the yen's rally through 121 per\par dollar aided sentiment in regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , but gains for\par some were capped by wariness of possible \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export competitiveness.\par     Although data from Singapore and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  bettered\par forecasts, analysts said the economic outlook was clouded by a\par lacklustre recovery in the United States -- export-driven\par Asia's largest market.\par     "Dollar weakness will support Asia regionals, but\par uncertainty surrounding the U.S. economy will at best keep most\par of them within ranges we have seen in the second half (of\par 2002)," said a senior dealer at a Singapore bank.\par     Those concerns pulled the Singapore dollar off Friday's\par three-month high of 1.7439 down to a session low of 1.7513 per\par dollar. The Sing strengthened back through 1.75, but dealers\par said fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would cap gains.\par  \par     "Most players are booking profits on the Sing dollar to\par preempt the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ," a European bank dealer said.\par     She said unless the Sing dollar strengthens beyond 1.7450,\par most players would feel safe in betting on a short-term\par retracement in the dollar.\par     The market largely ignored a surprising 1.8 percent annual\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rise in October retail sales, which analysts associated with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par more buoyant stock market and higher visitor arrivals for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par month rather than any improvement in domestic consumption.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par With the exception of a slight blip in July, Singapore's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par retail sales have been in a downward spiral all year as the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rising numbers of jobless keep a tight hold on their wallets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht touched fresh one-month highs at 43.18, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sentiment supported by the solid growth of gross domestic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par product in the year to the September, despite a slowing in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quarterly pace of growth.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The National Economic and Social Development Board said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy grew 5.8 percent over the year, faster than the 5.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent growth forecast by analysts and the 5.1 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year growth in the second quarter.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The agency forecast growth of 4.9 percent this year,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beating analysts' expectations, and 3.5 to 4.5 percent growth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in 2003.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso bucked the regional trend to fall to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 53.67 per dollar as demand for dollars from the offshore\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par non-deliverable forwards market outpaced the supply from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par overseas workers repatriating earnings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Manila said the peso could ease further as local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporates were hedging for a weaker \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the start of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par next year and exporters were holding onto their dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won posted its strongest close in five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weeks, tracking the yen's rise. The Taiwan dollar touched a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par one-month high early on, led by the yen, but gave up its gains\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on dollar buying by importers and concerns that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0814 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.49       121.74         +1.04\par  Sing dlr      1.7473       1.7489         +0.09\par  Taiwan dlr    34.792       34.835         +0.12\par  Korean won   1203.10      1210.00         +0.57\par  Baht           43.09        43.29         +0.46\par  Peso           53.64        53.55         -0.17\par  Rupiah       8805.00      8870.00         +0.74\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.49       131.24         +8.92\par  Sing dlr      1.7473       1.8515         +5.96\par  Taiwan dlr    34.792       34.986         +0.56\par  Korean won   1203.10      1277.00         +6.14\par  Baht           43.09        44.16         +2.48\par  Peso           53.64        51.50         -3.99\par  Rupiah       8805.00     10350.00        +17.55.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216dycg00iiy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22