\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Thai c.bank denies baht  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2002\par 07:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  (Recast with details) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, Oct 14 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was not concerned about the baht's slide to near nine-month lows and denied rumours the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the bomb blasts in Bali rippled through regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told Reuters the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the financial market on Monday to stop the baht's fall. \par \par \uc2  "The baht weakness is in line with other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , we have not touched it today," Pridiyathorn said. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said there had been rumours in the market of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The unit fell to an eight-and-a-half month low at 44.02 in early Asian trade. \par \par \uc2  By 0503 GMT, the baht was trading at 44.00/44.03 a dollar. \par \par \uc2  Overall sentiment toward Southeast Asian assets has worsened following the weekend bombing in Bali, which killed at least 183 and wounded hundreds, mostly foreign tourists. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the central banks of Indonesia and the Philippines \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to boost their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Thai Finance Minister Somkid Jatusripitak said recent debt repayments by the private sector had weakened the Thai baht, but the government was not concerned about the outflows. \par \par \uc2  "Many firms have constantly repaid their foreign debt, which has weakened the baht...but there is nothing to be worried about," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The latest data by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  showed foreign debt in the private sector fell by $516 million from June to $37.74 billion in July, compared with $45.8 billion in 2000. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021014dyae00bf9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
