\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Dulled by weekend,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  worries. \b0\par\par\uc2 535 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 2002\par 11:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 2 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were a mixed \par \par \uc2  bag in Friday trade, although a listless Japanese yen, the \par \par \uc2  approaching weekend and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept most from \par \par \uc2  rising much. \par \par \uc2      Regionals started the day firmer after weak U.S. economic \par \par \uc2  numbers undermined the dollar, but fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  wiped \par \par \uc2  out gains in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  baht and the Korean won \par \par \uc2  . \par \par \uc2      Traders were also unwilling to initiate positions before \par \par \uc2  the weekend with key U.S. unemployment numbers due later on \par \par \uc2  Friday, particularly after having seen two sets of dismal data \par \par \uc2  on growth and manufacturing this week. \par \par \uc2      "This is typical behaviour ahead of the weekend," Sameer \par \par \uc2  Goel, markets strategist with Bank of America, said. \par \par \uc2      "Given Asia's dependence on the United States, people are \par \par \uc2  also wondering if regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should be supported or \par \par \uc2  hammered if the United States does not do well." \par \par \uc2      Adding to that uncertainty were fickle equity markets, Goel \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        spent most of Friday in a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7540-1.7570 range, firmer than the previous day's close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7598 and with bullish traders seemingly daunted the fact that\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was close to being over-valued in trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par terms.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Korean won rose up to 1,176 before the concerns\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that won had appreciated too much compared with the Japanese\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par yen , which could threaten export competitiveness and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par invite \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , weighed and pulled it back to the day's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lows around 1,185.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won was also driven down by market talk that flows from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SK Telecom, which recently raised funds overseas through\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par American Depositary Receipts, are drying up.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fears were largely responsible for keeping the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  baht too narrowly bound. It gained briefly,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par spiking above 42 per dollar, but soon settled around Thursday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close at 42.13.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The finance ministry said on Friday there was no plan to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fire the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor, although earlier this week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra hauled up the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for letting the baht swing sharply.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso slipped to 51.30 by close, after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trading most of the day in a tight range of 51.10/15 per dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par despite talk of heavy foreign inflows from Philippine\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expatriates sending money home.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR AT 0910 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.94       120.07         +0.95\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.7598         +0.24\par  Taiwan dlr    33.723       33.667         -0.17\par  Korean won   1184.30      1182.80         -0.13\par  Baht           42.10        42.13         +0.07\par  Peso           51.27        51.15         -0.23\par  Rupiah       9080.00      9135.00         +0.61\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.94       131.24        +10.34\par  Sing dlr      1.7556       1.8515         +5.46\par  Taiwan dlr    33.723       34.986         +3.75\par  Korean won   1184.30      1277.00         +7.83\par  Baht           42.10        44.16         +4.89\par  Peso           51.27        51.50         +0.45\par  Rupiah       9080.00     10350.00        +13.99\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020802dy8200jay\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
