\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Track yen bounce, but cautious. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 683 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2002\par 04:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, July 19 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed \par \par \uc2  early on Friday, tracking the yen's bounce against the \par \par \uc2  dollar but reluctance to take aggressive positions ahead of the \par \par \uc2  weekend and wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was expected to keep \par \par \uc2  gains limited. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said players would be cautious after recent \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by central banks in Korea, Taiwan and \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \par \par \uc2  cap strength in their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and over uncertainty of the \par \par \uc2  dollar's near-term fate. \par \par \uc2      The dollar was down to around 115.80 yen at 0219 GMT, from \par \par \uc2  one-week highs at 117.30 overnight, in response to declines on \par \par \uc2  the Wall Street and on disappointing U.S. data on business \par \par \uc2  conditions. \par \par \uc2      "The market is uncertain on whether this wave of dollar \par \par \uc2  selling has been completed. As a result any dollar correction \par \par \uc2  will be volatile," said Thio Chin Loo, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Korean won         -2 rose to levels around 1,171.5 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from 1,174.8 where it finished in onshore trade on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said dollar sales by exporters was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushing the won higher, but players were wary of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of 1,170 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Taiwan dollar          edged up to around 33.03 per U.S.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from its onshore close of 33.04, but players were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par reluctant to test the 33 level beyond which the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to cap gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar        rose to around 1.7355 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from late Thursday's 1.7419, aided by dollar offers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from local corporates just beyond the 1.7400 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers said a lack of fresh local leads was likely to keep\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market focused on the dollar/yen moves and that another\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par test of 10-month highs beyond 1.7330 was possible if the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par declines beyond the 115.50 yen level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        rose to 40.47 per dollar, against late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday's 40.57, but dealers said the market lacked enthusiasm\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to push it much higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They said the market would not be able to count on bullish\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rhetoric from Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra after his\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par comments on late Thursday in which he said he would refrain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from commenting on the baht and leave the matter to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par \f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 \par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Thaksin had said on Sunday the baht would soon strengthen\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond the 40 per dollar level. The comment powered the baht to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-year highs around 40.20 before the rally was cut short by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah        surged to a over two-week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par highs at 8,785 per dollar on hopes of foreign inflows after the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank Restructuring Agency said on Thursday it expects up to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $3.4 billion in proceeds from the sale of non-performing loans.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        was slightly higher at 50.34 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, from its onshore close of 50.38, on moderate demand for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But dampening sentiment was fresh data showing the trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par surplus in the first five months of the year down 7.5 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the same period last year.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0221 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     115.83       117.10         +1.10\par  Sing dlr      1.7346       1.7419         +0.42\par  Taiwan dlr    32.996       33.040         +0.13\par  Korean won   1171.20      1174.80         +0.31\par  Baht           40.44        40.57         +0.33\par  Peso           50.33        50.38         +0.10\par  Rupiah       8790.00      8870.00         +0.91\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 