\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Governor: Baht Now Stable; Not Worrisome \b0\par\par\uc2 334 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Juli 2002\par 13:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Tuesday the level of the baht is now stable, despite the fact it hit a new 23-month high against the dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn said he wasn't concerned about the current level of the baht, although he didn't comment on earlier market talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the baht's appreciation. \par \par \uc2  "I am not worried about the baht and quite comfortable with it. The baht is stable now," Pridiyathorn told reporters. \par \par \uc2  He was relieved as the dollar regained some ground against the yen and the euro. \par \par \uc2  After the dollar touched an intraday low at THB40.28, it jerked up to THB40.40 in the afternoon in what traders suspect was an attempt by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the baht's rise. \par \par \uc2  However, the dollar soon resumed its slide in line with its general weakness against most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  However, Pridiyathorn said that the Thai baht was still in a managed float system, which means the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves the right to monitor and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to shape movements in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "\b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  is using the managed float system. But, I didn't say we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market today," he said. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn also noted the current baht level is still competitive for Thai exports. \par \par \uc2  "Nobody can predict the baht level. It will be decided by market mechanisms," he said. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn's comment came after Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra said Monday that the Thai baht would soon break below 40-baht to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The market took Thaksin's comments as a green light for faster baht appreciation, pushing the dollar sharply lower and breaking 41-baht to the dollar Monday before falling to a 23-month low of THB40.295 to the dollar at the end of Asian trade Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020716dy7g000pd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
