\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Stronger as dollar wobbles. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Anchalee Worrachate \par \uc2 829 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2002\par 05:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, June 21 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held on to \par \par \uc2  their strength in early trade on Friday as pressure mounted on \par \par \uc2  many fronts on the dollar. \par \par \uc2      But their appreciation were slowed somewhat by wariness of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by some central banks, which want to ensure their \par \par \uc2  local \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not move up too rapidly and threaten to \par \par \uc2  hurt export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2      Trading is expected to be lacklustre as players shift their \par \par \uc2  attention to the World Cup quarter-finals. England and Brazil \par \par \uc2  will slug it out at 0630 GMT while Germany and the United \par \par \uc2  States follow at 1130 GMT. \par \par \uc2      "People in the market seem to be talking more about the \par \par \uc2  World Cup than they do the dollar. I suspect the market might \par \par \uc2  come to a standstill in the afternoon...an unofficial half-day \par \par \uc2  holiday if you like," said a dealer at an Asian bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2      The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sank further across the board. Against \par \par \uc2  the yen, it extended losses to 123.30 after senior Japanese \par \par \uc2  Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the ministry \par \par \uc2  did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market following a sudden, \par \par \uc2  brief jump in the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has been fighting an uphill battle \par \par \uc2  against other majors for a while, was pressured further by news \par \par \uc2  of a record U.S. trade deficit and sliding stocks. \par \par \uc2  Its current account deficit - the broadest measure of \par \par \uc2  trade and service with foreign countries - hit a record \par \par \uc2  $112.50 billion, up sharply from a revised estimate of $95.10 \par \par \uc2  billion in the last quarter of 2001. \par \par \uc2  "I see the dollar's downtrend remaining intact in the very \par \par \uc2  near term. The area everyone is looking at is 122.80-123.00, \par \par \uc2  with the first being the last major \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  level. People \par \par \uc2  will be cautious when they get to those levels," said Andrew \par \par \uc2  Fung, head of treasury research at Rabobank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT TOP HEAVY \par \par \uc2  The Thai baht retained a firm tone, but bulls were \par \par \uc2  still reluctant to push it past the key 42 resistance amid talk \par \par \uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  However, some argued there was no incentive for the Bank of \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at this point given the baht still looked \par \par \uc2  fine on its nominal effective exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  "But we believe there is a good chance that if the \par \par \uc2  dollar/baht threatens to move below 41.90 without any \par \par \uc2  supporting dollar/yen decline, the Bank of Thailand will start \par \par \uc2  to become uncomfortable," said Rabobank's Fung. \par \par \uc2  The Korean won -2 traded near its morning high of \par \par \uc2  1,219.20 on the back of the dollar's decline against the yen, \par \par \uc2  but its upside was limited by government comments. \par \par \uc2  A senior Finance Ministry official said on Friday the \par \par \uc2  ministry was deeply concerned about the recent volatile moves \par \par \uc2  in the dollar/won rate and would take action to stabilise the \par \par \uc2  market if necessary. \par \par \uc2  RUPIAH UP ON IBRA TALK \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was supported by rumours that \par \par \uc2  the Bank Restructuring Agency (IBRA) sold dollars through local \par \par \uc2  banks. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted around 8,560/8,600 at 0315 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Sentiment was also boosted by IBRA's comments on Thursday \par \par \uc2  that it hoped to reach a $5 billion 2002 revenue target from \par \par \uc2  asset sales by September instead of year-end as part of efforts \par \par \uc2  to help reduce the state budget deficit. \par \par \uc2  The agency was set up during the Asian financial crisis in \par \par \uc2  the late 1990s to manage assets taken over from troubled state \par \par \uc2  debtors. \par \par \uc2  But the rupiah's rise is likely to be curbed by corporate \par \par \uc2  dollar demand and the fact that the market is pretty short of \par \par \uc2  the dollar at the moment, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar rose past the 34 to the dollar \par \par \uc2  threshold on the back of a firmer yen and the absence of the \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded around 33.854 - its 12-month \par \par \uc2  high - compared with 43.001 at the open and 34.023 at the \par \par \uc2  close on Thursday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0322 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.41       123.81         +0.32\par  Sing dlr      1.7746       1.7830         