\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up At 16-Mo High On Equity-Related Inflows \b0\par\par\uc2 654 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Juni 2002\par 11:57\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended firmer against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Tuesday thanks to equity-related inflows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 42.285 baht, its weakest level since February 2001. On Monday, it ended at THB42.41. \par \par \uc2  The dollar's bearish tone against most key \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also helped the baht, traders added. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at THB42.40, the day's high, and had been on a downward path since as offshore players and exporters continued to unload dollars, triggered by portfolio investment-related inflows. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors have been active net buyers on the Thai bourse recently. So far this month, they have bought a net THB4.01 billion worth of local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Moreover, the Bank of Thailand's tolerance toward the baht's recent gains also helped curb \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  jitters among market players. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Deputy Governor Pakorn Malakul Na Ayudhya said Tuesday that the baht's recent strength is in line with the dollar's weakness against other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  isn't concerned by the baht's real effective exchange rate against regional and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which is in line with the general trend. The real effective exchange rate is a measure of the country's export competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  "This comment shows that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is OK with the current baht level. That comforts most players to sell the dollar further," said a local dealer. \par \par \uc2  Traders expect the dollar to open Wednesday between THB42.20 and THB42.40, barring any sharp movements in the yen. \par \par \uc2  Thai long-term government bond prices rose slightly Tuesday on bargain hunting amid liquidity-driven demand, but failed to recover much of Monday's losses, traders said. Prices fell Monday on renewed fears of massive state-sector supply in the second half. \par \par \uc2  The short-term government bond due November 2004 ended in a bid-offer range of 2.45%-2.44%, down from 2.48%-2.46% at the close Monday. Bond yields and prices move in opposite directions. \par \par \uc2  The long-term issue due April 2010 finished at 5.03%-5.01%, down from 5.04%-5.02%. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand has said it will announce by the end of the month detailed plans for the issuance of up to THB320 billion in bonds by the state Financial Institutions Development Fund, or FIDF. \par \par \uc2  Unconfirmed reports from \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sources have said the issues will carry terms of 20 to 30 years, and that some of the total will be placed with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  or financial institutions. \par \par \uc2  The planned bonds should replace the FIDF's current short-term borrowings from financial institutions in the repurchase market. \par \par \uc2  The secondary bond market was expected to remain in a tight range in the near term. Any significant drop in yields before the end of the month is likely to invite sharp losses on occasional reports about the FIDF's issuance plans. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry auctioned Tuesday THB1.2 billion worth of 10-year government-guaranteed bonds to be issued by the state Expressway & Rapid Transit Authority, or ETA, at an accepted yield of 5.595%. The premium over the government bond yield curve was within expectations at just under 15 basis points. \par \par \uc2  Thai money market interest rates were mostly flat at low levels as the financial system remained flooded with excess liquidity. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank rate slipped to 1.875% from 1.9375%, as continued dollar selling began to contribute to financial institutions' baht liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market     Term                  Tuesday         Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most Active 1.8750%         1.9375%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close       1.6250%         1.6250%\par            14-Day                2.0000%         2.0000%\par            1-Month             no activity     no activity\par            3-Month             no activity     no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266\par 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020611dy6b000m4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
