\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Mostly firm, peso and won hit new highs. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 715 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2002\par 04:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, May 20 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held a \par \par \uc2  firmer tone early Monday while the dollar struggled to regain \par \par \uc2  some composure after last week's sharp falls. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said hopes of economic recovery and foreign inflows \par \par \uc2  in equity markets would push most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  higher, with \par \par \uc2  little or no threat of resistance expected by authorities. \par \par \uc2      "With Asian policy makers taking a more relaxed stance on \par \par \uc2  dollar weakness...the dollar continues to be re-rated \par \par \uc2  downwards," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS \par \par \uc2  Warburg in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      He said last week's implicit condoning of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength \par \par \uc2  by top finance officials in Korea, Singapore and Thailand would \par \par \uc2  encourage players to test their new tolerance levels this week. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, the dollar struggled off an early low of 128.18 \par \par \uc2  yen after Japan's top financial diplomat Haruhiko Kuroda \par \par \uc2  said there was no need for it to strengthen against the \par \par \uc2  greenback. \par \par \uc2      Senior Finance Ministry official Zembei Mizoguchi said the \par \par \uc2  ministry was always prepared to take action against excessive \par \par \uc2  moves in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2      Those comments prompted rounds of short-covering and \par \par \uc2  bargain-hunting from institutional investors, providing some \par \par \uc2  support to the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The euro        held firm at around 0.9200 cents against\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     PESO, WON HIT NEW HIGHS, RUPIAH DITHER\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Philippine peso        hit a 12-=   month high at 49.28\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar, backed by trade data showing a 10 percent jump in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par imports in March. The data raised hopes that the economy was on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its way to recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso ended offshore trade at 49.46 last Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to hit new highs early on Monday was the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean won -2. It touched a 15-month high of 1,253.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared to late Friday's 1,261.6, aided by a firmer yen and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, the Indonesian rupiah drifted slightly away\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from a test of 9,000 per dollar, a level it had not breached\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par since last September.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said strong corporate bids for dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par just ahead of 9,000 level prompted interbank players to cover\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some of their short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah eased to 9,080 from an early high of 9,060 and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Friday's 9,070. But dealers said most players expect a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par breach of the 9,000 level later in the day.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SGD & BAHT FIRM UP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar retested a seven-month high at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.7930, touched on Friday, with market focus on the dollar's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par losses against other major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Sing dollar was still supported by a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positive bias after recent economic data showed that a recovery\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was in the works.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But local corporates dollar bids around 1.7930-1.7940 was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capping gains for now.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar last Friday was around 1.8000 when the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strength was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within its policy parameters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Thai baht        rose to 42.60, from late Friday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 42.71, taking cue from the firmer tone in the yen and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the market was less concerned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap baht's rise, but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par commercial dollar bids were spotted ahead of 42.50, 15-month\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par high hit on Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0148 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     125.91       127.31         +1.11\par  Sing dlr      1.7936       1.7951         +0.08\p