\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Thailand says unconcerned by stronger baht. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nopporn Wong-Anan \par \uc2 490 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Mai 2002\par 13:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK, May 7 (Reuters) - Thai authorities said on Tuesday they were not concerned over the strengthening baht \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , classing its recent gains as temporary and unlikely to affect exports which are key to sustaining economic recovery. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the rise in the baht to 14-month highs had not hurt exporters, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  (BOT) would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The baht is not too strong. It still benefits exporters, since our (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) has only risen by 0.5 percent, compared with other countries' that have risen by two to three percent," Pridiyathorn told reporters. \par \par \uc2  "Therefore I see no need of taking any action." \par \par \uc2  Earlier, the baht was trading at 42.82/42.86 to the dollar, up almost three percent from a high of 44.13 on January 2. By 1130 GMT it slipped to 42.88/42.92. \par \par \uc2  Despite Pridiyathorn's confidence, dealers said the latest foreign reserves data - showing a rise of $400 million in a week to $34.60 billion as of April 26 - suggested the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  lately. \par \par \uc2  Commerce Minister Adisai Bodharamik said earlier on Tuesday the strong baht would not hurt exports, but that he preferred to see the unit weaken. \par \par \uc2  "I see the current strong baht as temporary and we can handle that...but it should be around 44 baht," Adisai told reporters. \par \par \uc2  Adisai said later there would only be cause for concern if the baht continued to remain strong over a longer period. "If the baht continues at the current level for some time, our exports will face a tougher time as their prices will rise." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the baht's strength was driven more by the direction of the dollar/yen rate than local factors. \par \par \uc2  "It's still a story of the dollar's weakness rather than the baht's strength," said Andrew Fung, head of treasury research at Rabobank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "Having said that, I must add the Thai economic outlook has improved, but I don't think that will be enough to stop the baht from weakening if the dollar/yen turns around," Fung said. \par \par \uc2  Thailand's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last week raised its forecast for economic growth this year to 2.5-3.5 percent from a previous projection of 2-3 percent, citing increased consumer spending and a faster global recovery. \par \par \uc2  But the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  scaled down its 2002 export growth projection to 1-3 percent from 3-4 percent after exports dropped a bigger than expected 6.3 percent year-on-year in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  In 2001, the economy grew 1.8 percent and exports, which account for about 55 percent of gross domestic product, slumped 6.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The finance ministry and International Monetary Fund have also raised their growth forecasts this month, to 3.6 percent and 2.7 percent respectively. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020507dy5700fa8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
