\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Ease with yen,  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  jitters. \b0\par\par\uc2      By Ovais Subhani \par \uc2 804 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 April 2002\par 04:09\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 30 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  easier early on Tuesday as the yen took a breather after \par \par \uc2  its recent run up to multi-month highs against the dollar. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The only exception was the Philippine peso        which\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continued its rally from Monday hitting fresh seven-month highs\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 50.60 per dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     In rest of the region, with the yen easing back to levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par beyond 128 per dollar from near two-month highs of 127.65,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players feared central banks might \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap any\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trade-weighted exchange rate gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Asian bulls need to be aware," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par UBS Warburg's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist in Singapore.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts say that with the export sector in most regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economies still in early stages of recovery, the recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rally could be quite near the threshold of their monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par authorities who are concerned about export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The recent net sale of local stocks by foreign equity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors in most Asian markets, part of which could end up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par chasing dollars, was also likely to offset any gains from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par usual month-end dollar sales by exporters.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Mohi-uddin said central banks of Singapore and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par might be the first ones to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in case of any sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gains, while equity-related dollar outflows have already\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par started to weigh down the Korean won and the Thai baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par CENTRAL BANKS SCARE\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar eased to hit a session low of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8107 from late Monday's 1.8063 as the dollar recovered some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lost ground against the yen and euro .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are a major component of the trade-weighted\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par basket of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  the Singapore authorities use to manage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par their exchange rate.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said players were covering short dollar positions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as some suspect that Monday's dollar purchases by local banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par starting from 1.8030-1.8020 range was for the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Those dollar purchases helped pull the Sing dollar down\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from 1.8010 six-month peak hit on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar has been in an upchannel since late March\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when it was around 1.8500 and has gained 2.42 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-to-date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Illustrating lingering worries over the pace of recovery,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Prime Minister Goh Chok Tong said late on Monday that cost\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pressures could weaken Singapore's recovery from recession and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par unemployment may reach 5.5 to 6.0 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Meanwhile, the Thai baht edged lower to 43.25 from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par late Monday's 43.18 as offshore players squared their short\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions ahead of economic data for March and revised\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  macro targets due later on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore said the market was waiting for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Bank of Thailand's view on the export sector outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     A weak exports outlook is likely to strengthen fears of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  that has kept the baht in a narrow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 43.10-43.20 range in the past several sessions. The baht has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gained over two percent year-to-date.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PESO PERKY, RUPIAH QUIET\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso briefly edged to 50.71 session low but perked up\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to around 50.63, a seven-month high hit on Monday, in response\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's bullish comments over the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Rafael Buenaventura said he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the peso to strengthen to 50.50 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The comment sent local players scrambling to cover their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short peso positions they had built in anticipation of violent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par protests by opposition parties on the Labour Day on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Indonesian rupiah was easier at around 9,350, from late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday's 9,310 as the positive impact of International Monetary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fund's approval of another $347 million loan tranche faded\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par away.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said the rupiah was expected to remain\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range bound especially amid thin trading interest ahead of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Labour Day holiday on Wednesday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S.       $0150 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     128.18       127.79         -0.30\par  Sing dlr      1.8093       1.8063         -0.17\par  Taiwan dlr    34.734       34.730         -0.01\par  Korean won   1283.60      1287.60         +0.31\par  Baht           43.22        43.18         -0.09\par  Peso           50.57        50.63         +0.12\par  Rupiah       9345.00      9310.00         -0.37\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     128.18       131.24         +2.39\par  Sing dlr      1.8093       1.8515         +2.33\par  Taiwan dlr    34.734       34.986