\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Powered ahead by yen, eyeing Greenspan. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,092 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 April 2002\par 11:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  basked in \par \par \uc2  the yen's limelight in late trade on Wednesday, with strong \par \par \uc2  gains in local stocks providing an extra boost. \par \par \uc2      The Korean won stole a thunder, surging by more than a half \par \par \uc2  percent to close at a five-week high after investors ditched \par \par \uc2  the dollar to cut losses against the backdrop of robust gains \par \par \uc2  in both stocks and the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar came off against the euro and the yen, partly \par \par \uc2  because a February report showed fund managers were turning \par \par \uc2  more constructive toward European assets at the expense of U.S. \par \par \uc2  assets which some thought were looking a bit overvalued. \par \par \uc2      The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also pressured by a vague rumour that \par \par \uc2  Federal Reserve chairman Alan Greenspan had resigned. \par \par \uc2      The Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took heart from the yen's resilience \par \par \uc2  in the face of Standard and Poor's downgrade of Japan which \par \par \uc2  suggested the market was long on the dollar, and that most \par \par \uc2  investors were not surprised by the move. \par \par \uc2  The market is waiting for Greenspan's testimony before a \par \par \uc2  Joint Economic Committee hearing on monetary policy and \par \par \uc2  economic outlook at 1400 GMT. \par \par \uc2  "What we have seen gradually throughout this year is that \par \par \uc2  Greenspan has become upbeat. It think we might see the \par \par \uc2  continuation of that trend," said Claudio Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  "And if we are very lucky, there might be some hint as to \par \par \uc2  when he may be thinking of the timing of a possible rate hike. \par \par \uc2  But again, don't expect too much. He likes to keep his \par \par \uc2  constructive ambiguity," he said. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won closed at a five-week high of 1,318.70 to the \par \par \uc2  dollar against Tuesday's close of 1,325.60, riding on the back \par \par \uc2  of the yen and local stock gains. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors bought a net of 265 billion won worth of \par \par \uc2  shares on the Korea Stock Exchange on Wednesday, the largest in \par \par \uc2  almost a month. They also bought a net 390 million won on the \par \par \uc2  over-the-counter Kosdaq. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Korea's new Finance Minister Jeon Yun-churl said \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday the government would decide on whether to alter \par \par \uc2  its expansionary economic policy stance in May after it reviews \par \par \uc2  first quarter growth data. \par \par \uc2  Salomon Smith Barney says in a report that it expects \par \par \uc2  "significant" monetary tightening in the second half of this \par \par \uc2  year, beginning in June. \par \par \uc2  "We now see official rates rising from 4 percent to 5 \par \par \uc2  percent by calendar year-end and to 5.5 percent 12 months hence \par \par \uc2  on strong economic growth and the policy constraint provided by \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own 2.5 percent core inflation target," it \par \par \uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose to test the psychologically key \par \par \uc2  1.8300 per U.S. dollar level, as it shrugged off a slightly \par \par \uc2  worse than expected headline non-oil export data for March. \par \par \uc2  The data showed a decline of 17.3 on the year, slightly \par \par \uc2  worse than a Reuters poll average of a 15.3 percent drop, but \par \par \uc2  was better than February's 23.4 percent slide. \par \par \uc2      In fact, on a three-month average seasonally adjusted \par \par \uc2  month-on-month basis, exports were up a marginal 0.8 percent. \par \par \uc2      Dealers said a lack of response to the data suggests the \par \par \uc2  Sing dollar would continue its rise beyond the 1.8300 where \par \par \uc2  stop-loss dollar sale orders are bunched up. \par \par \uc2      They said players trying to avoid trigger of those stops \par \par \uc2  were bidding up dollars at session highs around 1.8312, but \par \par \uc2  overall firmer regional tone and a steadier yen was drawing \par \par \uc2  dollar sales from others at around 1.8320. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah rebounded just ahead of the psychologically key \par \par \uc2  9,500 level on sporadic dollar offers suggesting that some of \par \par \uc2  the sovereign credit ratings downgrade risk, that had pulled \par \par \uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from recent highs near 9,300, might have already \par \par \uc2  been priced in. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Jakarta said moderate commercial dollar demand \par \par \uc2  and talk of more dollar sell orders beyond 9,500 may limit \par \par \uc2  rupiah's downside for now. \par \par \uc2  Still most interbank players were trying to cover their \par \par \uc2  dollar shorts amid wariness over Standard and Poor's threat of \par \par \uc2  downgrading Indonesia to "selective default". \par \par \uc2  The rating action is expected in response to government's \par \par \uc2  intention to force some private lenders to share the debt \par \par \uc2  rescheduling burden with the Paris Club of creditor nations. \par \par \uc2  The government is likely to restructure $340 million in \par \par \uc2  syndicated loans from private lenders after securing a rework \par \par \uc2  of $5.4 billion it owed to bilateral creditors. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso held on its tight range around the 51 per dollar \par \par \uc2  level as lack of fresh trading cues made players reluctant to \par \par \uc2  push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  either way. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Manila said dollar bids from corporates and \par \par \uc2  importers capped the peso's upside at around 50.95 session \par \par \uc2  highs, while players were reluctant to sell it far beyond 51 \par \par \uc2  per dollar amid a firmer regional tone, capping its downside at \par \par \uc2  51.025. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht edged higher as onshore players tried to catch up \par \par \uc2  with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's gains in the offshore market during the \par \par \uc2  Monday-Tuesday traditional New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  Dealers in Bangkok said talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar \par \par \uc2  purchases through Japanese names capped the baht's upside. \par \par \uc2  However, it managed to rise to its three-week high of 43.25. \par \par \uc2  Despite the rumours, Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn \par \par \uc2  Devakula denied the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow the \par \par \uc2  baht's gains against the dollar and said the baht's current \par \par \uc2  level was "satisfactory." \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0842 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     130.84       131.51         +0.51\par  Sing dlr      1.8291       1.8352         +0.33\par  Taiwan