\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Lower On Yen Weakness In Thin Trade \b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 April 2002\par 12:49\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended slightly lower against the dollar in Asian spot trade Thursday, tracking the movements of the yen in lackluster trade, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 43.53 baht, up from THB43.46 at the Asian close Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  opened at an intraday low of THB43.475, already showing the effects of the yen's early retreat back above Y131 against the dollar in early trade. A Japanese finance ministry official prompted dollar short-covering against the yen and other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  by predicting that the yen's recent rally was over. \par \par \uc2  "The pair (dollar/baht) was range-bound in quiet trade in the morning. Market participants stayed sidelined due to the local holiday mood and an absence of fresh factors to lead the direction," said a dealer. \par \par \uc2  Local markets will be closed Monday and Tuesday for the traditional Thai New Year holidays. \par \par \uc2  Volume rose slightly in the afternoon due to local corporate demand for dollars, especially from oil companies amid the recent increases in crude oil prices linked to the violence and the threat of further instability in the Middle East. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market unless the baht begins to strengthen against the yen, or on trade-weighted basis with a strong yen component. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has admitted to buying dollars on baht weakness in recent weeks, but denied Tuesday that it was in the market when the last serious test of dollar support at THB43.45 failed earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to open Friday in Asia in a range of THB43.45 to THB43.60. \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020411dy4b000un\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
