\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Chief:Baht Moving In Line With Market Trend \b0\par\par\uc2 191 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 April 2002\par 06:50\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to contain the baht's strength Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "We haven't done anything in the market. The baht is simply following the market trend," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  He was commenting on market speculation that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had stepped into the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the baht's excess appreciation after the dollar fell this morning below the 43.50 baht support level. \par \par \uc2  Asked whether the baht's strength will undermine the country's exports, Pridiyathorn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to closely monitor the baht's movement. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has indicated it will ensure that the Thai baht won't strengthen to a level that could hurt exports. \par \par \uc2  At 0505 GMT (1:05 EDT a.m.) the dollar was quoted at THB43.47, down from THB43.525 at Tuesday's close in Asia, following a sharp rise in the Japanese yen to below Y131 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020410dy4a000a1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
