\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  rally, inspired by yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,071 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 April 2002\par 10:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 4 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended \par \par \uc2  higher on Thursday, trotting after the resilient yen which \par \par \uc2  continued to vex and frustrate the dollar. \par \par \uc2      After a day of choppy trade that saw the dollar shoot above \par \par \uc2  the 133 yen mark, the dollar was trading a bit lower from its \par \par \uc2  late New York levels. The greenback has been suffering from the \par \par \uc2  slings and arrows of investors disgruntled over the lack of \par \par \uc2  outflows from Japan that many had expected. \par \par \uc2  Moreover a batch of soft data from the U.S. service sector \par \par \uc2  and the continuing violence in the Middle East contiued to nag \par \par \uc2  the dollar. The market's awareness that Japan and Europe would \par \par \uc2  suffer more from rising oil prices - a consequence of the \par \par \uc2  violence - provided the dollar little comfort. \par \par \uc2  There were local factors behind regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as \par \par \uc2  well. The Korean won continued to labour under foreign sales of \par \par \uc2  local stocks. And local corporate dollar demand thwarted the \par \par \uc2  Singapore dollar and Indonesian rupiah's rise. \par \par \uc2  As for regional monetary policy, the Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  decided to hold rates steady - a widely expected move. And \par \par \uc2  sticking to its neutral stance, the Philippine \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  said further rate cuts were unlikely given higher oil prices. \par \par \uc2  The Philippine economy got a small pat on the back from \par \par \uc2  ratings agency Standard & Poor's which raised its outlook from \par \par \uc2  negative to stable. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was once again shoved lower by investors upset over \par \par \uc2  another session of net selling of local stocks by foreign \par \par \uc2  investors. \par \par \uc2  Foreign investors disposed of a net 251.7 billion won worth \par \par \uc2  of shares on Thursday, the third straight day of selling. Even \par \par \uc2  though economist continue to hail Korea as one of the bright \par \par \uc2  spots in Asia as its economic recovery gathers pace, funds have \par \par \uc2  been cutting their positions in Korean shares and investing \par \par \uc2  elsewhere in Asia where they have less exposure. \par \par \uc2      However exporters' dollar sales saved the won from falling \par \par \uc2  much past the 1,330 level. \par \par \uc2      Meanwhile, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to keep its \par \par \uc2  overnight call rate as it is -- at four percent -- barely made \par \par \uc2  an impression in the market because it was widely expected. \par \par \uc2      The bank did warn of inflationary pressures, raising the \par \par \uc2  possibility that it might hike rates at its next month monetary \par \par \uc2  board meeting. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar kept to the stronger side of 35, aided by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a firmer yen and equity-related inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par      Dealers in Singapore said inflows related to stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par purchases by foreign investors from earlier in the week may\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par continue to trickle in for a few more days as the transactions\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par are settled and support the Taiwan dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and Wednesday's sales of local equities by foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors made players reluctant to push the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors were net sellers of 309 million Taiwan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar worth of local stocks on Wednesday after buying a net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 26.53 billion of shares in the previous 11 sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar tracked the firmer yen but ran into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar bids from local players near its session high of 1.8400.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said the Sing dollar's downside was checked by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign names spotted unwinding long dollar positions beyond\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the 1.8420 level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They said the absence of fresh news has left the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par focused on dollar/yen moves though uncertainty over yen's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par near-term direction was expected to keep the dollar well-bid.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was slightly higher tracking the yen and other\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par regionals. But local corporates kept a lid on its upside\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par keeping it away from testing the 51 per dollar level.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Merchandise export data for February showed a 6.4 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par decline on the year, but the decline was smaller than previous\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par falls and raised hopes of a gradual recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market shruged off Standard & Poor's upgrade of outlook\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on Philippines long-term ratings to stable from negative citing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par tighter budget management.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the move was already factored in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after S&P announced its intention last month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    S&P affirmed Philippines triple-'B'-plus long-term and 'A-2'\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term local and double-'B'-plus long-term and single-'B'\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sovereign credit ratings.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah climbed higher thanks to steady dollar sales\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from foreign names who were eyeing investment flows into\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indonesia's telecom giant PT Telkom confirmed it had signed\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a deal with Singapore Telecommunications to sell a 12.7 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stake in its cellular unit, Telkomsel. The stake amounts to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par US$429 million in cash.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The deal would reduce Telkom's holding in Telkomsel to 65\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent and raise SingTel's ownership to 35 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Corporate dollar bids, however, slowed the rupiah's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par progress. And charts showed the rupiah's gains may soon be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par capped as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been consolidating around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,640-9,840 range so far this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht held onto its firmer tone, following the regional\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par trend higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was off the session's best of 43.59\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because of wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said on Thursday that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he was concerned about the country's export performance and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible impact from the baht on trade flows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief said it would act to reduce the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par obstacles that were hindering trade, but he did not specify.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0815 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     132.44       132.79         +0.26\par  Sing dlr      1.8398       1.8436         +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    34.999       35.002         +0.01\par  Korean won   1330.40      1329.00         -0.11\par  Baht           43.60        43.71         +0.25\par  Peso           51.12        51.15         +0.07\par  Rupiah       9670.00      9760.00         +0.93\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     132.44       131.24         -0.91\par  Sing dlr      1.8398       1.8515        