\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Clouded by yen, Middle East woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,088 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2002\par 11:18\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 1 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mostly \par \par \uc2  weaker in late trade on Monday as players snapped up dollars \par \par \uc2  against the backdrop of a weaker yen and brewing tensions in \par \par \uc2  the Middle East. \par \par \uc2      The yen dipped across the board, hurt by a disappointing \par \par \uc2  Japanese business "tankan" survey which showed no improvement, \par \par \uc2  and speculation investors were likely to buy foreign assets now \par \par \uc2  that the financial year was out of the way. \par \par \uc2      The regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were also edgy due to conflict in \par \par \uc2  the Middle East which the market feared could jack up oil \par \par \uc2  prices and hurt growth prospects as well as current accounts of \par \par \uc2  oil-dependent Asian countries. \par \par \uc2      "The direct impact will be felt through the oil prices, \par \par \uc2  especially for those countries which are net importers of oil \par \par \uc2  like Japan and Korea, although you might argue the impact on \par \par \uc2  Japan might not be severe given its deflation," said Claudio \par \par \uc2  Piron, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Standard Chartered in Singapore. \par \par \uc2      The Middle East tensions escalated after Israeli forces \par \par \uc2  stormed Ramallah, The Palestinian Authority's base, and other \par \par \uc2  West Bank cities at the weekend following a spate of \par \par \uc2  Palestinian suicide bombings. \par \par \uc2      Asia's oil consumption is estimated at around 21 million \par \par \uc2  barrels per day (bpd) while the region can produce only around \par \par \uc2  8.5 million bpd, leaving a production-consumption shortfall of \par \par \uc2  around 12.5 million bpd. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Sing dollar flirted with its multi-month lows seen last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week on the back of a weaker yen and the listless local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, but its losses were capped by profit taking near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8480.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Last week the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  fell to 1.8510 -- its worst\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level since January 10. Trading was subdued as Hong Kong and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par London markets are closed on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, dealers expect the Sing dollar's downside to be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par limited in the near and medium-term as charts show the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par is trading at the lower end of its nominal effective exchange\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rate (NEER) band, indicating upside risk ahead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The market barely reacted to money supply data released on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Saturday which showed bank credit in February dipped slightly\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to S$160.73 billion from S$160.93 billion in January while M1\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par money supply rose to S$36.47 billion from S$35.80 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht sank to the intraday low of 43.61 after the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par took the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief's remarks and the recent export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data to mean the authority might be in favour of a weaker baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula told\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Reuters the bank would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if needed in the foreign\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets to stave off volatility in the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which had risen sharply in recent months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Meanwhile, exports fell 8.1 percent on the year in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par February. The country's improving current account surplus was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par due partly to a sharp decline in imports which raised doubt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about investment recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won fell a notch from Wednesday's close of 1,325.9,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ending at 1,327.5 on importer dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Losses on the local share market also weighed on sentiment\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par towards the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Despite net purchases by foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors during Monday's session, their sales on Friday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weighed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Seoul traders also said some foreign players were still\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par seeking to repatriate proceeds from dividend payments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, more evidence of Korea's economic rebound came in,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fuelling speculation as to whether the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raising rates soon to temper inflationary pressures. While\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par exports fell in March, it was the smallest decline in a year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moreover, the new \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Park Seung said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy was expected to grow by around five percent this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par An official at the bank said it would adopt a flexible approach\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to setting its rate target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah edged higher from its day's worst level of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,800, though corporate and foreign bank dollar bids were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worrying it.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  opened around the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,800 level, but was quickly rescued by across-the-board dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, local corporates jumped in to buy the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around the its day's low of 9,660, with foreign banks also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par eagerly bidding in the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Volume was relatively heavy for this chronically thin\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, with dealers estimating some $300-$400 million changing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hands.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "Whoever has the biggest flow is determining the market,"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said a foreign bank dealer in Bangkok.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Indeed, there was a noticeable absence of fresh factors,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the market impervious to political developments and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expecting Jakarta to secure a key debt rescheduling deal with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its Paris club of foreign creditors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government released some poor economic figures that\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par showed year-on-year inflation still in double digits and the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par country's trade surplus falling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended at 35.00, unchanged from Friday's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  shook off any jitters from the huge\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earthquake that struck the island on Sunday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Damage from the earthquake was minimal, although five\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par people were killed and over 200 injured.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been helped by healthy inflows into the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stock market. However, wariness over \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meant it did not venture far from the 35 mark.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Since the end of last year, the bank, which \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par both sides of the market, has kept the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around the 35\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level. Taiwan is starting to emerge out of one of its worst\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recessions, and the bank is doing what it can to keep the rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stable as the island gets back on track.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0848 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.21       133.01         -0.15\par  Sing dlr      1.8468       1.8430         -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr    35.002       35.000         -0.01\par  Korean won   1327.50      1325.90         -0.13\par  Baht           43.58        43.51         -0.16\par  Peso           51.00        51.01         +0.01\par  Rupiah       9740.00      9800.00         +0.62\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.21       131.24         -1.48\par  Sing dlr      1.8468       1.8515         +0.25\par  Taiwan dlr    35.002       32.900         -6.01\par  Korean won   1324.90      1277.00         -3.62\par  Baht           43.58        44.16         +1.33\par  Peso           50.99        51.50         +1.00\par  Rupiah       9740.00     10350.00         +6.26\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020401dy4100h4y\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
