\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  mixed, eye on yen,equities. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,079 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 April 2002\par 04:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, April 1 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were \par \par \uc2  mixed early on Monday as markets around the region re-opened \par \par \uc2  after the Easter holiday. \par \par \uc2      The tensions in the Middle East were haunting the market, \par \par \uc2  which was anxious that escalating violence in the region could \par \par \uc2  lead to a spike in oil prices. Most Asian countries, with the \par \par \uc2  exception of Indonesian and Malaysia, are net oil importers. \par \par \uc2      Still, players were keeping an eye on the two main driving \par \par \uc2  forces behind Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  -- the yen and equity inflows. \par \par \uc2      In the bigger picture, analysts expect the regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to do well in the long run as global growth picks \par \par \uc2  up. As a major exporter, Asia is expected to benefit from \par \par \uc2  sharpening consumer appetites. \par \par \uc2  Still, there was a catch - the temperamental yen. \par \par \uc2  "Like commodity \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asian markets remain favoured \par \par \uc2  as trades on global growth. But with the JPY continuing to be \par \par \uc2  volatile, the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  remain buffeted against the \par \par \uc2  USD," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS \par \par \uc2  Warburg in Singapore in a research note. \par \par \uc2  He advocated sticking with \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  less exposed to the \par \par \uc2  yen's fickle ways - the Thai baht and Philippine peso - with \par \par \uc2  an eye on better entry levels for the more liquid \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  such as the Korean won, Taiwan dolllar and Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar kept its weak tone against the U.S. dollar \par \par \uc2  alongside the yen, languishing near the 1.8450 level. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar, like other regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was clouded by concerns over the brewing tensions \par \par \uc2  in the Middle East which, if escalated, would affect oil \par \par \uc2  prices. \par \par \uc2      The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also weighed by equity outflows to \par \par \uc2  other countries in the region, they said. \par \par \uc2      "If the 1.8450 doesn't hold, the next target that we are \par \par \uc2  looking at is 1.8500," said a dealer at an Asian bank in \par \par \uc2  Singapore. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht retreated below the 43.50 level, reflecting a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weaker yen which prompted interbank players, especially some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Japanese names, to cover short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But its downside was underpinned by fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and some improvement in the February data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakul told Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  would \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  if needed in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets to stave off volatility in the Thai \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which had\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par risen sharply in recent months.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On the data front, current account surplus in February rose\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to $989 million from $332 million in January. Its manufacturing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par index also edge up by 2.4 percent on the year from a revised\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.5 percent in January.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened slightly firmer at 51.050 to the dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par compared with 51.005 on Wednesday on the back of demand from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par interbank players who had oversold the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a long Easter holiday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was thin, with only $3.5 million traded as of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0128 GMT as players waited for fresh leads after the Easter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par break.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  drew mild support from news of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government eyeing a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  swap agreement with China and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par South Korea to boost its dollar reserves as a precautionary\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par measure against potential financial market shocks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Under the planned arrangement, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may borrow\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollars in exchange for the local \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to meet urgent local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par demand for the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won rose slightly from Friday's close of 1,325.9 thanks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to exporters' dollar sales.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the market was keeping a close eye on the activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of foreign investors in the stock market. It was anxious about\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par whether foreign investors would be net sellers of local shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign flows have had the biggest influence on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par direction in recent sessions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors sold a net 29.6 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Korean shares on Friday. So far on Monday, they've bought a net\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9.7 billion won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall, though, analysts and dealers said the won should\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par appreciate over time as the Korean economy steams ahead. Of all\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Asian economies, the market has been trumpeting Korea\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because of its resilience during last year's slowdown and its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par relative structural soundness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     But rising oil prices could thwart the sunny outlook for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Korean economy, which relies heavily on oil imports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was not far from its Friday levels of around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 9,800, but dealers said players were looking to cover their\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par short dollar positions.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Jakarta said there were few new factors in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, with sentiment towards the rupiah still upbeat. While\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market was keen to cover their short dollar positions after\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the re-emergence of local corporate dollar demand late last\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, players were likely to sell the dollar on rallies.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market was also keeping an eye on crucial debt talks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par between Jakarta and the Paris Club of official creditors later\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par this month.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR          The Taiwan dollar moved down a notch\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from Friday's close of 35, following the softer yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Sentiment towards the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also shaken by a strong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par earthquake on the island on Sunday, which left five people dead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and 272 injured. Taiwan shares dipped on panic-selling, despite\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par no reports of major damage.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was unlikely to stray too far from the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 35 level, where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has kept it pinned to. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank has been active on both sides of the market to ensure a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stable rate while the island's economy slowly wends its way\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down the road of recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0132 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change