\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 forex \highlight\uc2  takes holiday breather. \b0\par\par\uc2 925 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 02:37\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 29 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took \par \par \uc2  a breather in light, holiday trade on Friday, with many of the \par \par \uc2  region's major \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading centres closed for the \par \par \uc2  Easter holiday. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  whose markets were open for trade notched \par \par \uc2  lower, with the yen and equity flows dominating the Korean won \par \par \uc2  and Taiwan dollar and wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  keeping a lid on the Thai baht's upside. \par \par \uc2      But trading in those market was relatively subdued. \par \par \uc2      Markets in Singapore and Hong Kong, as well as Manila and \par \par \uc2  Jakarta were closed for Good Friday. With the exception of Hong \par \par \uc2  Kong, they will re-open on Monday. Hong Kong reopens on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2      In the bigger picture, analysts were trying to divine the \par \par \uc2  fate of the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as evidence of a healthy \par \par \uc2  rebound in the U.S. continued to come in and the dollar/yen \par \par \uc2  remained in familiar territory. \par \par \uc2      While recent fears of a potential rate hike in the U.S. did \par \par \uc2  cause Wall Street to fret about the possibility of tightening \par \par \uc2  liquidity -- in turn, hurting the dollar -- some analysts said \par \par \uc2  a rate hike would ultimately support the dollar. \par \par \uc2      "The implications of an earlier rate hike from the Fed and \par \par \uc2  a firmer growth performance in Q1 implies a steady USD against \par \par \uc2  Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said BNP Paribas in a research note. \par \par \uc2      Rate hikes usually support a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because they mean the \par \par \uc2  assets denominated in that \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would be more attractive to \par \par \uc2  investors. Last year, however, because of the slowing global \par \par \uc2  economy, the market viewed rate cuts by the Federal Reserve as \par \par \uc2  dollar supportive because it heightened hopes for a speedy \par \par \uc2  rebound. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won eased a tad to 1,328.5 to the dollar at the open as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it shadowed the weaker yen. It later rebounded to 1,327.3,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par still slightly weaker than Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also hurt by dollar purchases from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par importers with bids for the greenback connected to recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity sales knocking around in the market as well.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However a number of factors were supporting the won.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Firstly, foreign equity net selling had reversed in recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions after a hefty sell-off.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Secondly, analysts' view that Korea was one of the most\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par attractive places in Asia to park money was underscored by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moody's Investors Service's move to up the country's foreign\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ceiling for bonds and noted by two notches on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday. That decision puts Korea on par with China, Hong Kong\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and Hungary.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The ratings agency cited the country's sound fiscal\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par position, and praised the government's policies and reform\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par efforts.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The baht fell from Thursday's late levels of 43.44 to trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around 43.52 to the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Bangkok dealers said importers and corporates were looking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to for dollars in a market that was still unnerved by the Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  governor Pridiyathorn Devakula hinted that it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par had been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to curb the baht's gains in order to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par maintain export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors have been net sellers of local stocks for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the past three sessions, though they remain net buyers of 18.5\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion baht of Thai stocks so far this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar edged lower on the back of the yen's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fall, and was back on the wrong side of 35.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was not expected to see any sharp\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par moves given the looming and likely possibility of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . Taiwan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  on both sides of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market on a regular basis to keep the exchange rate stable.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     For the past three months, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has kept within a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par narrow 34.88-35.167 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar mimicked the yen's losses, but to a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lesser extent given the holiday-thinned trade, to trade around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8431/41.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Singapore markets are closed and will reopen on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah fell a rung or two in thin offshore trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Jakarta markets were closed and will re-open on Monday. On\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had given up its recent strong gains as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bargain hunters and corporates snatched up the dollar.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  also fell after the Indonesian Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Restructuring Agency said it received around $320 million in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par payment for a 30 percent stake in Bank Central Asia. Players in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market had been betting on those inflows flooding the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, which they have yet to do.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso was steady in minimal offshore trade. Manila\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets have been closed since Wednesday and will re-open on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0120 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     133.01       132.56         -0.34\par  Sing dlr      1.8430       1.8395         -0.19\par  Taiwan dlr    35.010       35.009          0.00\par  Korean won   1327.00      1327.00          0.00\par  Baht           43.51        43.44         -0.16\par  Peso           50.97        51.15         +0.34\par  Rupiah       9800.00      9780.00         -0.20\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995          0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     133.01       131.24         -1.33\par  Sing dlr      1.8430       1.8515         +0.46\par  Taiwan dlr    35.010       34.986         -0.07\par  Korean won   1327.00      1313.00         -1.05\par  Baht           43.51        44.16         +1.49\par  Peso           50.97        51.50         +1.04\par  Rupiah       9800.00     10350.00         +5.61\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020329dy3t002hq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
