\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Asian  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  ease with yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,110 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 03:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  eased a \par \par \uc2  tad early on Wednesday, dragged lower by a weaker yen. \par \par \uc2      Falls on Wall Street, particularly in technology stocks, \par \par \uc2  were also likely to vex the North Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which were \par \par \uc2  already coping with the yen's stumble. \par \par \uc2      However, analysts noted that the extent of the regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' falls has been muted. Indeed, with the exception of \par \par \uc2  the Korean won, all the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have gained against the \par \par \uc2  dollar since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  Moreover while Japanese authorities have been busy trying \par \par \uc2  to prevent the yen from rising too far, too fast, Asian central \par \par \uc2  bankers have been relatively subdued about recent gains. The \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  once again said on Tuesday it would not \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to temper the baht's recent rise, adding it did not \par \par \uc2  hurt exports. \par \par \uc2  "I think the region is getting comfortable right now ... \par \par \uc2  The U.S. is on the mend and the dollar/yen's collapse last week \par \par \uc2  just shows there's no danger for now of 140 or 150," said \par \par \uc2  Philip Wee, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at DBS Bank in Singapore. \par \par \uc2  The market was keeping its eye on Federal Reserve Chairman \par \par \uc2  Alan Greenspan's speech on Wednesday, which is the day when key \par \par \uc2  data on U.S. retail sales in February will also be issued. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht dawdled in a narrow 43.10-43.30 range in a dearth \par \par \uc2  of fresh leads from both the dollar/yen and the stock market. \par \par \uc2  "The baht seems to be consolidating around that band as the \par \par \uc2  dollar/yen and the stock market are settling into range as \par \par \uc2  well," said a dealer at a local bank in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht was unlikely to rise above 43.00 - a \par \par \uc2  barrier not broken since February 2001 - any time soon unless \par \par \uc2  the yen strengthens towards 127 and more capital inflows enter \par \par \uc2  the market. \par \par \uc2      The onshore overnight interbank rate was steady at around \par \par \uc2  1.95-2.00 percent. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah froze in a tight 9,925-9,985 band as the market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lacked the resolve to push it either way while awaiting news of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the winning bid for the government's sale of a majority stake\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Bank Central Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was subdued, with dollar offers from foreign banks\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par offset by corporate dollar demand.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The government said on Tuesday the winner of the sale would\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not be announced later in the day as was previously hoped.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par State Enterprises Minister Laksamana Sukardi said he hoped the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par winner could be announced by later this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The sale of the bank is seen as a crucial test of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government's commitment to economic reform and its willingness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to push through divestment of assets to foreigners in the face\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of domestic opposition.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won slipped on concerns over equity-related outflows\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because of five consecutive sessions of net selling by foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said repatriation of profits by some\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par multinational companies was also adding downside pressure on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the won. One U.S. bank was spotted buying dollars on Tuesday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for such repatriation requirements.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors sold a net 124.8 billion won worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local shares on Tuesday amid talk the investment was flowing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par into Japanese and other Asian assets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said those concerns had prompted most interbank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par players to build up long dollar positions. They said the won\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was expected to ease into a weaker 1,315-1,323 range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso opened a tick higher at 50.84 after settling at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 50.87 on Tuesday, supported by favourable budget deficit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par On Tuesday, Budget Secretary Emilia Boncodin said the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par government was expected to meet its 130 billion pesos ($2.55\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion) budget deficit target for this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Still, some dealers in Manila were sceptical about the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pledge, saying they would have to wait for the final figures as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par public spending plans to boost the economy could push the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit to 52.9 billion pesos in the first quarter, or 40.6\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent of the year target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They added the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  faced resistance around the 50.80\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level where dollar orders from some manufacturing clients were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lined up. They also noted corporate demand for pesos was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lacklustre.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Overall, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was poised to trade above the key 51\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par level for the next few sessions because corporate investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par have not hedged their dollar positions and thus will pressure\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the peso lower.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "The current levels are a true blessing to them (the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate investors)," a Manila-based trader said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was supported by equity-linked inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the pace of those inflows has moderated in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par past few sessions while a softer yen was also expected to cap\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par any significant upside for the currrency.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Singapore added few players were interested in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pushing the Taiwan dollar higher from current levels around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 34.95 after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent dollar-buying\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to protect export competitiveness.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, if the yen stays within 128-130 range, dealers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to drop.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors bought a net T$1.89 billion worth of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par local shares taking their net buying over the past nine\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions to T$46.59 billion.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar crept slightly lower, silently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par shadowing the yen.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Trading was lacklustre with few other factors in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, dealers said. With more activity and higher gains in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the major \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the market in the dollar/Sing has thinned\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par out.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers said there were still players looking to exit long\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar positions, which were taken above the 1.8300 level. That\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meant the dollar was likely to run into stiff resistance around\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1.8240/45 for now.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0136 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     129.12       128.56         -0.43\par  Sing dlr      1.8215       1.8204         -0.06\par  Taiwan dlr    34.958       34.947         -0.03\par  Korean won   1320.60      1318.50         -0.16\par  B