\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Mostly firmer as yen recoups losses. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,073 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2002\par 11:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, March 12 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  crept \par \par \uc2  higher in late trade on Tuesday after the yen clawed \par \par \uc2  back some gains against the dollar on the back of exporter \par \par \uc2  dollar sales. \par \par \uc2      Expectations of more inflows into regional assets also \par \par \uc2  supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2    The Thai baht was among the star performers, nudging higher \par \par \uc2  on  capital inflows and comments by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it \par \par \uc2  saw no need to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to slow down its gains. \par \par \uc2      The yen recovered some lost ground after falling to a \par \par \uc2  session low of 128.88 due to losses in the stock market \par \par \uc2  and talk that the government plans to buy a large amount of \par \par \uc2  foreign bonds in fiscal 2002. \par \par \uc2      Most analysts are betting that the yen will resume its \par \par \uc2  sustained weakness after the book closing season is over by the \par \par \uc2  end of this month. \par \par \uc2      "We do not believe that strength in the yen will be \par \par \uc2  maintained. It is true that a global economic recovery and \par \par \uc2  (recent) rallying Japanese stock market are usually positive \par \par \uc2  for the yen. The sustainability of the strength of the stock \par \par \uc2  has to be questioned, however," said a JP Morgan note. \par \par \uc2      "It is a result of official manipulation -- including \par \par \uc2  government buying and short-sale restrictions -- rather than \par \par \uc2  optimism about restructuring," it said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The rupiah was trapped in a narrow range of 9,950-9,990\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while players waited on the sidelines for news of the winning\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bid for the government's sale of its majority stake in Bank\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Central Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Jakarta-based dealers said trading was light, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate dollar demand balanced by dollar offers from foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par banks.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     They added the market kept its cool when the government\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said the winner of the sale would not be announced later in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par day as was previously hoped. State Enterprises Minister\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Laksamana Sukardi said he hoped the winner could be announced\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by later this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Local media had reported the possible delay, which meant\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market was prepared for this announcement, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par They also expressed confidence that the deal would go through.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     THAI BAHT        The baht strode higher, rising above the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 43.15 level on the back of the firmer yen and dollar offers\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from exporters who feared the baht would strengthen further.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also bolstered by comments by the Bank of\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which reiterated on Tuesday it would not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the market to slow down the baht's recent sharp rise which it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said was in line with other regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers say there was speculation in the market earlier\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was likely to enter the market to curb\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the baht's appreciation if it rises past 43.00 where hefty\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stop-loss orders from players with long dollar positions are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lining up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     KOREAN WON         -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The won succumbed to foreign net sales of local stocks,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the wobbly yen also hurting sentiment towards the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Foreign investors were net sellers of local stocks for the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fifth consecutive session in a row, dumping a net 124.8 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par won worth of shares.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Analysts say with the global outlook improving, funds are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par looking to park their money elsewhere. Korea benefited from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par huge inflow of foreign funds at the beginning of the year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par because it is seen as one of the more stable economies in Asia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But analysts say that also left more room for a correction in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local stock market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Still, the Korean Composite Stock Price Index         has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par gained nearly 22 percent since the start of the year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par     The Singapore dollar        pared earlier gains on profit\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par taking, but remained supported by the yen's rebound and hopes\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par for more inflows ahead.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers say despite some consolidation in the local stock\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market, they expect more upside ahead on the back of economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par recovery.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore unit, largely dependent on the yen's daily\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par activity, traded tightly between 1.8185-1.8210, with traders\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par suggesting the band was likely to stay narrow amid the dearth\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of market-moving factors to trade on.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar ended slightly higher despite losses in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the local stock market and a wobbly yen, thanks to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par equity-related inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investors bought a net 1.89 billion Taiwan dollars\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth of local shares taking their net buying over the past\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nine sessions to 46.59 billion Taiwan dollars.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     However, the stock market ended down 1.19 percent tracking\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Nasdaq's losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     That kept the overall tone of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trading soft with a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session low of 34.985. Players were also reluctant to push the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  higher after \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's recent \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cap\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's upside.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged higher to end its onshore trade at 50.87 per\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar from Monday's close at 50.99 amid talk of equity-and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par investment-linked inflows.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was also supported by a brighter outlook of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the fiscal position. The government said it has secured $2.8\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion this year in development assistance from international\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par donors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Budget Secretary Emilia Boncodin said the government was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected to meet its 130 billion pesos ($2.55 billion) budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit target for this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, front loading of public spending plans to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stimulate the economy could push the deficit to 52.9 billion\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par pesos in the first quarter, or 40.6 percent of the full\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-year target.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     She said the deficit was expected to taper off in the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par succeeding quarters.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0840 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     128.56       128.96         +0.31\par  Sing dlr      1.8204       1.8224         +0.11\par  Taiwan dlr    34.947       34.949   