\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends A Tad Higher In Line With Yen's Recovery \b0\par\par\uc2 256 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2002\par 11:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended a tad higher against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Friday, tracking the Japanese yen's slight recovery, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar finished at 44.03 baht, down slightly from THB44.065 at the Asian close Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The dollar was stuck in a very tight THB44.02-THB44.05 range in quiet intraday trade due to the relative lack of volatility in the yen, the regional trendsetter. \par \par \uc2  Thai exporters and debtors held back their respective dollar sell and buy orders ahead of the weekend, waiting for a clearer direction in the yen next week, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The market shrugged off a local newspaper report Friday in which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Assistant Governor Tarisa Watanagase was cited as saying that the bank has occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula had said late Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  In any case, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  against market trends, and the amount of dollars purchased by suspected agents of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last week wasn't significant, a foreign bank trader said. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be buying dollars on weakness to build foreign reserves and that Pridiyathorn may not consider this to be \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The dollar was expected to open Monday in a range of THB43.90-THB44.10, subject to any renewed volatility in the yen. \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020111dy1b000lz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
