\par\par \b \uc2  THAI PRESS: Ctrl Bk Admits  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt In 02 \b0\par\par\uc2 208 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2002\par 02:17\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has admitted occasionally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market this year, buying dollars to help stem the baht's volatility, the Nation reports, quoting the bank's Assistance Governor Tarisa Watanagase. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered into the market to prevent the baht trading from too much volatility. However, we don't need it (the baht) to move against the market trend," Tarisa was quoted as saying by the newspaper. She didn't disclose the amount of dollars bought. \par \par \uc2  She said after a period of weakening, the strength in the baht over the past few days was in line with movements in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . There were no other special factors affecting the Thai baht recently. \par \par \uc2  Contrary to the newspaper report, Bank of Thailand Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn was apparently responding to market talk late last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought dollars through a bank in Singapore to curb the baht's strength. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    Newspaper Web site: \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.nationgroup.co