\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk Governor: Haven't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 139 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2002\par 12:00\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said late Thursday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathorn was apparently responding to market talk late last week that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had bought U.S. dollars through a bank in Singapore to curb the Thai baht's strength. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is quite stable. But we will continue to monitor the market closely," Pridiyathon said. \par \par \uc2  Asked about the baht trend in the future, he said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  doesn't want the baht to be volatile. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted at 44.065 baht in late Asian trade Thursday, barely changed from THB44.06 at the previous close. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020110dy1a000n4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
