\par\par \b \uc2  Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Mixed Late As Yen Takes A Breather \b0\par\par\uc2  By Netty Ismail \par \uc2 886 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2002\par 10:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed late Thursday after clambering off their intraday lows, as expressions of concern by Japanese monetary officials over the speed of the yen's recent decline provided the beleaguered Japanese unit with some breathing space. \par \par \uc2  The yen's slide to as low as Y133.24 to the dollar early Thursday had cast a shadow on the other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, regained their footing when the yen recovered on comments by a senior official at Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Zembei Mizoguchi, and subsequently Finance Minister Masajuro Shiokawa, expressing concerns over the pace of the yen's recent declines to three-year lows. \par \par \uc2  Their comments came at a time when Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi is on the second day of his five-nation tour of Southeast Asia - during which he risks being bombarded with complaints over Japan's weak yen policy. \par \par \uc2  Unlike some of their North Asian counterparts, Southeast Asian officials have remained silent despite worries that further pressures on their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a slumping yen could push up the costs of servicing the region's dollar-denominated debts and dampen their economies' recovery prospects. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has bounced off the psychologically important Y132 level to trade around Y132.40 at 0910 GMT, lower than Y132.65 late Wednesday in New York. \par \par \uc2  "Dollar/yen's failure to break Y132 is a good sign," said a dealer at a European bank. "For all you know, dollar/regionals will trend back up again." \par \par \uc2  Indeed, the dollar remained buoyed above the psychologically important levels against Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as participants took advantage of the U.S. unit's pullback to add on to their long U.S. dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Against the Singapore dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stayed above S$1.8400, and was quoted at S$1.8436 late in the day, compared with S$1.8467 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "The Singapore dollar has been the most correlated with the yen's movements," said Mansoor Mohi-uddin, a regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at UBS Warburg. "But it's beginning to show signs of outperforming." \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's recent move to reinstate a narrower policy band within which it guides the trade-weighted local dollar indicates that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be less tolerant of the Singapore dollar's weakness against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Philippine peso in part received a boost from investors' overwhelming response to the government's 15-year global bond issue, which was increased to $750 million from $500 million, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "With the fresh borrowing, the government needs to raise less than $400 million to complete a $1.4 billion foreign financing requirement for 2002," which is needed to help it finance an estimated 130 billion-peso budget deficit this year, BNP Paribas said in a report. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of foreign investment inflows from the sale of shares in food conglomerate San Miguel Corp. (Q.MGL) to Japan's Kirin Brewery Ltd. (KNBWY) also bolstered the peso, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The peso also found support from remittance inflows from Filipinos working overseas and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decision to leave overnight rates unchanged. \par \par \uc2  The dollar closed at PHP51.325 on the Philippine Dealing System, down from PHP51.560 Wednesday. Volume almost doubled to $125.2 million from $69.7 million Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  After floundering to as low as 1,318.0 won to the dollar in early trade, the South Korean \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended at KRW1,312.3, only marginally lower than Wednesday's close of KRW1,311.9. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a high of KRW1,318.0 after the dollar rose to just short of the three-year high against the yen set Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Korea Governor Chon Chol-hwan said Thursday that the current level of the yen was "not too worrisome," despite his concern over the direction of the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  He added that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market unless market volatility increases "excessively." \par \par \uc2  The won shrugged off the Bank of Korea's as-expected decision to keep the overnight call rate unchanged in January at 4%. \par \par \uc2  Against the New Taiwan dollar, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at NT$35.025, slightly lower than NT$35.050 Wednesday, in dealings valued at US$584.5 million. \par \par \uc2  To keep a rein on the appreciation of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - in an apparent bid to maintain the price competitiveness of Taiwan's exports - the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  snapped up more than US$100 million throughout the session, dealers in Taipei said. \par \par \uc2  The Thai \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was slightly weaker at 44.100 baht to the dollar, compared with THB44.065 late Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  "There are fears in the market that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be coming in to buy dollars if it falls sharply below THB44," said Mohi-uddin at UBS Warburg. Late last week and early this week, there were market suspicions that the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the strength of the baht as it traded past THB44. \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unchanged from late Wednesday's level of around 10,430 rupiah to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Netty Ismail, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-415-4043; netty.ismail@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020110dy1a000jh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
