\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Attuned to U.S. hopes,but down w/yen. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,000 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 November 2001\par 03:29\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 30 (Reuters) - The yen's overnight losses \par \par \uc2  clouded Friday's forecast for Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , though the \par \par \uc2  yen's usual cohorts in North Asia were likely to stay steady. \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dolllar and Korean won have not been much \par \par \uc2  affected by the dollar/yen's movements, focusing on \par \par \uc2  developments on the local front while the two major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  squabbled over a bit of territory. \par \par \uc2  In Korea, investors remained fixated on the local stock \par \par \uc2  market's direction with foreign investment flows determining \par \par \uc2  where the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be headed. But Wall Street's gains, \par \par \uc2  after news that U.S. durable goods rose in October, were likely \par \par \uc2  to buoy Korean shares. \par \par \uc2      The Taiwan dollar has held up ahead of key parliamentary \par \par \uc2  elections on Saturday. \par \par \uc2      Local events on Friday were few, with Korea saying \par \par \uc2  November's consumer price index fell on month and the Bank of \par \par \uc2  Thailand announcing monthly forward economic indicators. \par \par \uc2      Friday also marks the adjustment to the Morgan Stanley \par \par \uc2  Capital International indices, which was expected to have a \par \par \uc2  limited impact because it was long anticipated. \par \par \uc2      The market, however, was keeping its eye on a preliminary \par \par \uc2  read on third-quarter U.S. gross domestic product. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     SINGAPORE DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Singapore dollar tagged after the yen, and was trading\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par close to its overnight lows of around 1.8330.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Of all the regional \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the Singapore dollar has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been the most loyal to the yen with players still favouring a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par stronger dollar/Sing.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Daily charts showed the dollar/Sing consolidating, keeping\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par within a range of 1.8267-1.8343. Dealers said unless the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/yen made any rapid moves in either direction, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar/Sing was likely to remain within this range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par KOREAN WON -2\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The won kept close to its levels late on Thursday, with the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par market expecting stock-related inflows and month-end exporter\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales to lift the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Sentiment was also boosted by news that Moody's Investors\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Service raised the outlook for Korea's Baa2 sovereign debt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rating to positive from stable. Standard & Poor's recently\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par raised the country's long-term foreign \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rating to BBB+.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market shrugged off news that October's CPI recorded a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0.5 percent month-on-month drop - the first monthly drop this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year. Analysts say, however, benign inflation could persuade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Bank of Korea to ease its overnight call rate next week\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when it holds its monthly rate-setting meeting.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah dawdled around its recent levels, hoping local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par corporate dollar demand would remain around its recent levels.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market has remained relatively subdued in recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sessions, dealers in Jakarta said. Nevertheless, the rupiah has\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par not been able to gain much ground due to the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weakening fundamentals.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government said on Thursday inflationary pressure was\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par hitting the economy hard. And as another signal of flagging\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par confidence in the economy, Fitch said it had changed its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par outlook for Indonesia's ratings to stable from positive.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The government also continued to push ahead with its race\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to dispose of assets ahead of year-end. Jakarta said it will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par announce its decision about a closely-watched plan to sell a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par majority stake in PT Semen Gresik to Mexico's Cemex. That plan\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par has so far been thwarted by provincial governments.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par THAI BAHT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The baht was on the wrong side of the 44 per dollar mark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with players reluctant to push it higher on talk of possible\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is due to release monthly economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par data on manufacturing, trade and current account balance and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par its monetary policy committee will review key domestic interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said recent gains in regional\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , especially the Singapore dollar, and equity-related\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows were supporting the baht.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But speculation that the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , to protect export\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par competitiveness, may not allow the baht to appreciate above the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 44 level has prompted players to square out of long baht\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par positions at around 44.05.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has repeatedly said it would not cut its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par benchmark 14-day repurchase rate, now at 2.5 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula on Thursday said an\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par adjustment in interest rates would not be needed unless the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par economy looked to be slipping below its forecast growth range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of 1-3 percent for 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The peso edged above the 52 level in light offshore trade\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with local markets closed for a holiday. Manila markets will\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par resume trade on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Singapore said players next week will focus on a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par possible interest rate cut and rising remittances from overseas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par workers may further help the peso higher.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar nudged higher on hopes of month-end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales by exporters but fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dollar\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par buying \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and uncertainty ahead of Saturday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par parliamentary elections was expected to limit gains.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par More downward pressure on the Taiwan dollar may come from\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected equity-related outflows after foreign investors sold a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par net 1.90 billion Taiwan dollar worth of local stocks on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday halting a five-session net buying streak.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0145 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     123.92       123.09         -0.67\par  Sing dlr      1.8325       1.8295         -0.16\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       34.465         +0.01\par  Korean won   1259.00      1270.50         +0.91\par  Baht           44.08        44.06         -0.05 #VALUE!\par  Rupiah      10390.00     10402.00         +0.12\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     123.92       114.45         -7.64\par  Sing dlr      1.8325       1.7365         -5.24\par  Taiwan dlr    34.460       32.900         -4.53\par  Korean won   1259.00      1277.00         +1.43\par  Ba