\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Higher On Continued Cap Market Inflows \b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 November 2001\par 11:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended higher in Asian spot trade Tuesday, supported by inflows of investment funds to local capital markets, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar was quoted in late trade Tuesday at 44.075 baht, down from THB44.15 at the Asian close Monday. \par \par \uc2  Offshore players have been selling dollars to invest in equity and bond markets over the past week, Bangkok dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Foreign net buying in Thai stocks continued Tuesday, and payment - in baht - was due Wednesday for the THB15 billion worth of bonds to be issued by local mobile phone operator Advanced Info Service. Much of the THB10 billion allotment to institutions was believed to have gone to offshore parties. \par \par \uc2  "Continued inflows from foreign investors have pressured the dollar against the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , despite its strength against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," a foreign bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. unit has risen in recent days against the Japanese yen and the Singapore dollar. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar hit an intraday low of THB44.06 soon after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced Tuesday it will maintain the policy-signal 14-day repurchase market interest rate at 2.5%. \par \par \uc2  The decision to leave the rate unchanged was expected, but eliminated a factor which might have supported the dollar for at least the medium term. \par \par \uc2  Bank of Thailand said it could make its monetary policy more accomodative if the economic recovery was weaker than expected, but it said fiscal stimulus would help to keep gross domestic product growth in the forecast range of 1%-3% next year. \par \par \uc2  Dollar weakness was limited by local corporate demand from importers and those with foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 -denominated debts, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expect resistance at THB44.15 Wednesday. Firm support is expected at THB44.00, underpinned by concerns over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem volatility, and of accumulating dollars to maintain foreign reserves while repaying loans taken out under an expired International Monetary Fund rescue program. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bonds finished slightly higher Tuesday on liquidity-driven demand after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's affirmation of no change in current monetary policy reduced uncertainty over the market's near-term direction. \par \par \uc2  The issue due October 2005 finished in a bid-offer range of 3.62%-3.60%, down from 3.66% at the close Monday. The July 2007 issue finished at 4.20%-4.18%, down from 4.215%. Yields move in the opposite direction to prices. \par \par \uc2  Yields should continue to edge lower Wednesday, when the first auction of new three-year and 10-year government bonds will be held. The secondary market yield curve suggested that results would be in a range of 3.2%-3.3%, and 5.2%-5.3% respectively. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  auction will also reopen an existing government bond issue due April 2021 for THB1.5 billion. No activity was reported in the issue Tuesday, but results in Wednesday's auction should be around the most recent quotations near 6.20%. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity-driven demand should continue to underpin sentiment in the near term, but there wasn't a lot of room for yields to fall before persistent support levels were encountered again, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Money market interest rates closed mostly flat amid ample liquidity. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market      Term                    Tuesday      Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most Active    2.4375%      2.4375%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close          2.1250%      2.0625%\par            14-Day                   2.5000%      2.5000%\par            1-Month                no activity    2.5625%\par            3-Month                no activity    2.6250%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Supunnabul Suwannakij and Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires;\par 662-266-0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011127dxbr000lv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
