\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Weaker vs U.S. dollar on war news. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,051 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 November 2001\par 09:40\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Nov 14 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Wednesday \par \par \uc2  were mostly softer against the U.S. dollar, which was boosted \par \par \uc2  by hopes of a speedy conclusion to the war in Afghanistan and \par \par \uc2  fears of Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to weaken the yen. \par \par \uc2      The Thai baht bucked the trend, rising on the back of \par \par \uc2  capital inflows linked to investment in the equity market, with \par \par \uc2  gains exaggerated somewhat by thin market volumes. \par \par \uc2      The U.S.-supported Northern Alliance captured the Afghan \par \par \uc2  capital of Kabul on Tuesday, causing soldiers for the ruling \par \par \uc2  Taliban regime to scatter. The news bolstered the U.S. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which had been hurt by the plane crash in New York on \par \par \uc2  Monday. \par \par \uc2      But the market was reluctant to push the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  too \par \par \uc2  far due to fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2      There was talk of Taiwan's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  entering the \par \par \uc2  market \par \par \uc2  to sell the U.S. dollar at 34.52 and of Bank Indonesia selling \par \par \uc2  the greenback to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Trading in the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  was thinned by a market \par \par \uc2  holiday in Singapore. Financial markets in the city state will \par \par \uc2  reopen on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Investors are awaiting U.S. retail sales numbers due out later \par \par \uc2  on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Economists polled by Reuters forecast a 2.7 percent \par \par \uc2  increase in October retail sales, with strong auto sales \par \par \uc2  driving gains in the headline figure after a 2.4 percent \par \par \uc2  decline in September. Excluding autos, retail sales are seen \par \par \uc2  gaining 0.2 percent after a 2.4 percent decline in September. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON \par \par \uc2  The won tallied up some gains thanks to the local stock \par \par \uc2  market's rise and renewed net buying by foreign investors. \par \par \uc2  Foreign equity-related flows, more so than the direction of \par \par \uc2  the dollar/yen, have held sway over the won in the past few \par \par \uc2  weeks. While Tuesday's net sales of local stocks drove the won \par \par \uc2  lower, signs of a pick-up in net buying by foreign investors \par \par \uc2  cheered the won. \par \par \uc2  Still, a softer yen did impede the won's rise, though the \par \par \uc2  market managed to shrug off news that the country's \par \par \uc2  unemployment had risen by an adjusted 3.5 percent in October \par \par \uc2  compared with 3.3 percent in September. \par \par \uc2  It was the first rise in eight months, with analysts and \par \par \uc2  officials saying the ranks of the unemployed were likely to \par \par \uc2  swell in coming months. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht remained well-supported by capital inflows which \par \par \uc2  dealers said were likely to be linked to the IPO of a local \par \par \uc2  state-run energy company later this week. \par \par \uc2  But its upside was capped by the dollar's strength against \par \par \uc2  other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reign in its gains. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  relies heavily on exports, which account for more \par \par \uc2  than 50 percent of its gross domestic product, and a strong \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  can hurt its competitiveness. \par \par \uc2      Baht funding costs in the offshore market were generally \par \par \uc2  firmer, with the one-month forward rate quoted at 6/10 satang \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par per dollar.      PHILIPPINE PESO\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso crawled off its intraday low of 52.18 to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, thanks to rumoured \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Dealers in Manila said the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  might have sold\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around $10-20 million to defend the peso below 52.10.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The peso weakened after corporate players snapped up the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to cover short positions and to repay foreign\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Inflows from overseas Filipino workers had been scarce this\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par week, which may confirm analysts' predictions that inflows are\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par likely to slow this year because of the global economic\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slowdown and rising unemployment.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In the bond market, rates on government securities fell by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as much as 25 basis points in the secondary market as demand\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par picked up due to excess liquidity in the system.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier in the day, Finance Secretary Jose Camacho said he\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par expected the 91-day T-bill rate to remain below 10 percent for\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the rest of 2001.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par INDONESIAN RUPIAH\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The rupiah rose above 10,600 after some players unwound\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par long dollar positions partly due to fears of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Dealers in Jakarta said the market had overbought the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar late last week on anticipation that a few local\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par companies would buy big amounts, but the demand turned out to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par be lower than expected.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Any reprieve is likely to be short-lived as there is no\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par lack of bad news in Indonesia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the political front, the market was still jittery over\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par potential violence after a prominent pro-independence leader in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the troubled province of Irian Jaya was found dead over the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Foreign investment approvals in January-September fell to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $6.05 billion from $12.25 billion last year. Investors have\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par been avoiding Indonesia for months due to concerns over its\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par political and economic instability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Taiwan dollar stayed within the bounds of its recent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range, and idled around the 34.50 mark in dozy trade.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For weeks, the local dollar has not ventured far from a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par range of around 34.50-34.60 because of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's near\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par daily presence. Foreign stock-related inflows, exporters'\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar sales and even negative economic news have failed to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bump the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  out of its range.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts say the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been remarkably\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par successful at keeping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  stable, which it is\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par determined to do to hold onto Taiwan's export competitiveness\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par while not damaging domestic sentiment.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0811 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     121.44       121.24         -0.16\par  Sing dlr      1.8251       1.8250         -0.01\par  Taiwan dlr    34.504       34.505         +0.00\par  Korean won   1282.00      1273.00         -0.70\par  Baht           44.37        44.42         +0.11\par  Peso           52.15        52.09         -0.12\par  Rupiah      10565.00     10670.00         +0.99\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     121.44       114.45         -5.76\par  Sing dlr      1.8251       1.7365         -4.85\par  Taiwan dlr    34.504       32.900         -4.65\par  Korean won   1282.00      1277.00         -0.39\par  Baht           44.37        43.70         -1.51\par  Peso           52.15        50.75         -2.68\par  Rupiah      10565.00      9470.00        -10.36\par  Ringgit       3.8000       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011114dxbe00gzj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
