\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Lower, Rate Cuts Help Dlr; Ctrl Bk Fears \b0\par\par\uc2 422 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2001\par 13:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht ended lower Tuesday as the dollar found support from interest rate cuts overnight by several major central banks, including the U.S. Federal Reserve, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The central banks' resolve to stabilize the markets and protect the global economy helped calm nerves in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets. \par \par \uc2  As reported, the U.S. Fed cut its federal funds rate by 50 basis points. \par \par \uc2  The dollar finished at 44.235 baht, up from THB43.975 at Monday's Asian close. \par \par \uc2  Milder-than-expected losses on Wall Street also helped sentiment. The Dow Jones Industrial Average lost 7.1% Monday, while the Nasdaq Composite Index tumbled 6.8%. \par \par \uc2  Fears of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , amid talk that it had bought the dollar below the THB44 level Monday, also gave a boost to the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  However, dealers said the dollar remains directionless due to uncertainties over the possible U.S. retaliation against the perpetrators of last week's terrorist attacks. \par \par \uc2  Reports that the ruling Taliban had urged Afghans to prepare for a holy war against the U.S. should it attack, also weighed on the dollar movements. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the dollar is expected to trade in a range of THB44.10-THB44.40 Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  Thai government bonds ended barely changed as news of worldwide interest rate cuts was offset by concerns of a possible "holy war" against the U.S., traders said. \par \par \uc2  Yields, which move in the opposite direction to prices, fell by an average of six basis points in the morning in response to the interest rate reductions by the Federal Open Market Committee and other key central banks. \par \par \uc2  "But, yields started to rise later on market jitters after Taliban news," a local bank dealer said. \par \par \uc2  According to the Thai Bond Dealing Center's report, the most active December 2006 issue closed up at 5.38% versus 5.34% at the previous close, while the July 2007 issue closed flat at 5.48%, the report said. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai overnight interbank rates ended lower after their recent sharp\par rise on easier liquidity after the central banks' moves.\par Market      Term                   Tuesday     Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most Active   3.2500%     3.7500%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close         2.3125%     2.3125%\par            14-Day                  2.5000%     2.5000%\par            1-Month                 no activity no activity\par            3-Month                 no activity no activity\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Supunnabul Suwannakij and Suttinee Yuvejwattana; Dow Jones\par Newswires; 662-266-0744; supunnabul.suwannakij@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010918dx9i000su\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
