\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Ctrl Bk: THB Stable, Hasn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  In  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Mkt \b0\par\par\uc2 226 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 September 2001\par 12:23\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devekula said Friday that the baht has been stable so far, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market. \par \par \uc2  "There is nothing to worry about. The baht's strength is in line with the global (\b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) market," he told reporters. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar has fallen against most \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the terrorist attacks in the U.S. Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Pridiyathon said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will monitor the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, especially when the U.S. stock market resumes trading, expected Monday. \par \par \uc2  However, he said panic selling of U.S. stocks is expected to be minimized, because the U.S. markets have been closed after the attacks, so the impact of Tuesday's events on the market when it opens is unlikely to be catastrophic. \par \par \uc2  He added that the recovery in European and key Asian bourses Friday after their recent declines also signaled that the impact of New York markets, when they do open, won't be that serious. \par \par \uc2  At Friday's Asian close, the dollar finished at 44.245 baht, down from THB44.290 at the previous close, on continued dollar selling in the aftermath of the terrorist attacks in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  -By Suttinee Yuvejwattana, Dow Jones Newswires; 662-266-0744; suttinee.yuvejwattana@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument d