\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Higher as dollar languishes. \b0\par\par\uc2 999 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 2001\par 04:24\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 31 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  stood firm early on Friday as falls on Wall Street and an interest rate cut by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  badly bruised the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Even with poor economic news spilling out of Japan and the rest of the region, the market remained more compelled by the bearish news from the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The Dow Jones Industrial Average slipped past the key psychological threshold of 10,000 and the Nasdaq fell past 1,800 - lows not seen since April. \par \par \uc2  While U.S. equity losses could drive local stock markets lower, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at best have risen slightly with the yen or remained stable at worst. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said while most of the action has been in the euro , the yen's resilience has made the dollar vulnerable to the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "Logically, the Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  should weaken against the euro and dollar given the fundamentals, but I'm not willing to bet on it at these levels," said a U.S. bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar rose with the yen, breaking 1.7395 for the first time since February 27 despite local banks' agressive U.S. dollars bids. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the market suspected these banks were acting on the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's behalf as the authorities may be concerned about the Sing dollar's appreciation on a trade-weighted basis. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say with the city-state in a technical recession, the MAS was unlikely to tolerate further strength in the Sing dollar against the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said Hong Kong-based banks were selling dollar/Sing on the back of the yen's gains. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won eked out gains on the stronger yen, but losses on the local stock market prevented it from rising much higher. \par \par \uc2  Anxiety over local developments prevented the won from strengthening beyond 1,280. Local stocks fell as investors fretted over the fate of Hynix Semiconductor. \par \par \uc2  Creditors of the debt-laden chip maker have delayed talks on rescuing the company. \par \par \uc2  The market was also watching for July industrial output production due at 0300 GMT. A Reuters poll showed analysts on average expect a 0.9 percent month-on-month drop in July. \par \par \uc2  It reacted little to the rise in August's consumer price index of 0.5 percent from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht climbed in line with the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  with local and foreign banks unwinding their long dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said the baht had hit a high so far of 44.18 against 44.29 in active trade. They added, however, the dollar should find support around 44.10, which is close to the low it hit on August 28. \par \par \uc2  While some in the market thought the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  around the 44 level given the country's tottering economic fundamentals, dealers said it was unlikely. \par \par \uc2  "The baht is moving in line with the regionals, and the authorities have said before they will tolerate that," said a local bank dealer in Bangkok. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah edged up in line with the regionals on wariness over \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was suspected to have sold dollars on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  But Singapore dealers said demand for the dollar from local corporates for debt repayment needs was high and would weigh the rupiah back down to the wrong side of 9,000. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been in the market since the rupiah fell through the 9,000 mark earlier this week. \par \par \uc2  Finance Minister Boediono said on Thursday the government was considering a stronger exchange rate of 8,000-9,000 per dollar for the 2002 budget. A rate of 9,600 per dollar was assumed for the 2001 budget. \par \par \uc2  The government is expected to submit to parliament key economic assumptions for the 2002 budget in September. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso gained ground, helped by a firmer regional tone and on month-end export-related inflows. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said with a stronger yen and expected export inflows, most corporates and importers were likely to stay on the sidelines and an upward break of the 51 mark was possible. \par \par \uc2  The peso was just shy of the 51 mark, facing covering of short dollar positions. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also detering importers from entering the market. They added low trading volume was exaggerating moves. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was slightly firmer, tracking other regionals and the yen, but Hong Kong dealers said pressure on the U.S. dollar was light and no big deals were reported. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a high of 34.55 in morning trade against Thursday's close of 34.582. \par \par \uc2  Dealers had not heard of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far on Friday, but added the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may step in around 34.50. The Taiwan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been spotted buying U.S. dollars to stem the local dollar's rise. \par \par \uc2  Analysts and dealers say the authorities are keen on maintaining export competitiveness. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0220 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     118.85       119.76         +0.77\par  Sing dlr      1.7385       1.7473         +0.51\par  Taiwan dlr    34.558       34.582         +0.07\par  Korean won   1281.00      1283.50         +0.20\par  Baht           44.17        44.29         +0.27\par  Peso           51.05        51.22         +0.32\par  Rupiah       8895.00      8900.00         +0.06\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     118.85       114.45         -3.70\par  Sing dlr      1.7385       1.7365         -0.12\par  Taiwan dlr    34.558       32.900         -4.80\par  Korean won   1281.00      1277.00         -0.31\par  Baht           44.17        43.70         -1.06\par  Peso           51.05        50.75         -0.59\par  Rupiah       8895.00      9470.00         +6.46\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010831dx8v000xg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
