\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Gains stalled by dollar reprieve. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,087 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 August 2001\par 11:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Aug 17 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  lost steam after recent strong gains as the yen retreated against the dollar late Friday following a series of comments by Japanese officials which sparked fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts reckoned dollar weakness would continue but mostly against the euro rather than the yen as Japan's economy is too weak to withstand a strong \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "We have set the U.S. dollar trade-weighted weakness on our \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  forecasts to come primarily against the euro, not against the yen," said Adam Le Mesurier, regional economist at Goldman Sachs in Singapore, in a report. \par \par \uc2  "We still look for the yen to depreciate in the near-term. This combination means non-Japan Asia \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will still need to weaken both in trade-weighted terms and also against the dollar to buffer them from a severe external shock," he said. \par \par \uc2  The market was also driven by local factors. The Singapore dollar lost ground after July trade data showed non-oil domestic exports (NODX) fell 24.2 percent on the year. \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar ended easier on local media reports suggesting second quarter growth data would be worse than expected, a view that was borne out after the market's close. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar pulled back as the yen's retreat and bearish export data prompted players to buy the U.S. dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the worst was yet to come for non-oil exports which contracted 24.2 percent on the year in July. \par \par \uc2  "There has not been a definite sign of a rebound in U.S. demand or an upturn in activities in the U.S. manufacturing sector," said Syetarn Hansakul, economist at WestLB. \par \par \uc2  "Secondly, retained imports, which are a good leading indicator for NODX continue to decline, falling 17.6 percent year-on-year in July," she said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers expected the Sing dollar to find a toehold around 1.7500 if the yen stayed around 120 to the dollar. It hit a 5-= month high of 1.74 when the yen surged past 120 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  TAIWAN DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar slipped from Thursday's close of 34.52 as dealers bought dollars after local media reported second-quarter gross domestic product fell a worse-than-expected two percent year-on-year. \par \par \uc2  After the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market closed, the statistics bureau said Q2 GDP contracted 2.35 percent, well below the average 0.30 percent contraction forecast in a Reuters poll. It was the first decline in 26 years. \par \par \uc2  A statistics agency official said the 2001 growth forecast had been slashed to a 0.37 percent contravction from a previous forecast of 4.02 percent growth, made in May. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  called an impromptu news conference at 0930 GMT to announce a quarter percentage point cut in key interest rates. It has already lowered rates by 1.25 percentage points since late last year in an effort to get the economy going. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht nudged lower alongside the yen as dollar offers by onshore parties were outpaced by bids from offshore players, dealers in Bangkok and Singapore said. \par \par \uc2  Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market this week but would monitor the baht's movement to keep it stable. \par \par \uc2  The baht has gained more than 1.50 percent this week. A strong technical barrier is expected at 44.40, the 38 percent retracement of the dollar's February 2-April 9 rise. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, Prime Minister Thaksin Shinawatra rebuffed an IMF suggestion that Thailand should not rule out interest rate cuts, saying rates were already low enough. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso slipped past 51 to the dollar in thin trade as local corporate dollar demand emerged around 51.10. \par \par \uc2  Manila dealers said trading was subdued given the market's fear of more attempts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to shore up support for the peso. \par \par \uc2  "It's local factors that are moving the market now. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has made it clear it's not a sin to sell dollars, it's a sin to buy dollars," said a local bank dealer in Manila. Government offices and state-owned firms were closed around noon due to flooding in metro Manila. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official told Reuters the bank also closed most of its departments. \par \par \uc2  But traders said this had little impact on trade. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won closed lower on dollar buying from importers and a state bank. But it was not clear if the state bank's purchases were on behalf of clients or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Its presence at around 1,280-1,282 prompted other commercial banks to cover short dollar positions, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, data released on Friday showed the consumer confidence index fell in July after rising for six consecutive months, suggesting a poor outlook for consumption in the second half of this year. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was quoted at 8,700/8,800 in the offshore market, with trade at a virtual standstill as Jakarta markets were closed for a public holiday. They will re-open on Monday. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Sjahril Sabirin told reporters earlier in the day the rupiah was still undervalued. He added an acceptable level for the rupiah was 7,000-8,000 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  Analysts say the new government has to tackle the country's many economic problems effectively before the rupiah can make further headway. \par \par \uc2  Since President Megawati Sukarnoputri took office, the rupiah has gained around 30 percent on rising hopes the new government will begin mending the shattered economy. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  0942 GMT \par \par \uc2   Change on the day \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currency\b0 \highlight\uc2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     120.40       119.27         -0.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7530       1.7419         -0.63\par  Taiwan dlr    34.541       34.520         -0.06\par  Korean won   1285.00      1272.00         -1.01\par  Baht           44.74        44.48         -0.58\par  Peso           51.15        50.95         -0.39\par  Rupiah       8725.00      8725.00         +0.00\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     120.40       114.45         -4.94\par  Sing dlr      1.7530       1.7365         -0.94\par  Taiwan dlr    34.541       32.900         -4.75\par  Korean won   1285.00      1277.00         -0.62\par  Baht           44.74        43.70         -2.32\par  Peso           51.15        50.75         -0.78\par  Rupiah       8725.00      9470.00         +8.54\par  Ringgit       3.7998       3.7995         -0.01.\par \f28 \par \par \