\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  - Out of the yen's shadow, for now. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,037 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2001\par 10:48\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      SINGAPORE, Aug 14 (Reuters) - Most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  struck \par \par \uc2  an upbeat note late on Tuesday, even as the yen floundered, \par \par \uc2  following the Bank of Japan's surprise decision to further ease \par \par \uc2  ultra-loose monetary policy. \par \par \uc2      Dealers pegged further position unwinding, amid the \par \par \uc2  dollar's general weakness against other major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as \par \par \uc2  the reason for the bout of strength in regionals. \par \par \uc2      The Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  racked up the greatest \par \par \uc2  gains, though thin liquidity in the peso, rupiah, and baht \par \par \uc2  markets exaggerated their rises. \par \par \uc2      "You have to consider the open positions out there. At the \par \par \uc2  beginning of the year, the most obvious trade is selling \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  and going underweight in local stocks," \par \par \uc2  said a senior European bank dealer in Hong Kong. \par \par \uc2      "So given that, the recent dollar weakness, and the summer \par \par \uc2  holidays -- it's clear we are in a corrective phase." \par \par \uc2      But he and others said a weaker dollar does not bode well \par \par \uc2  for Asia given the region's dependence on exports to the U.S. \par \par \uc2      More yen weakness was also poised to weigh on regional \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it would increase already cut-throat export \par \par \uc2  competition. The yen slipped after the BOJ unexpectedly \par \par \uc2  announced its decision to ease already loose monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  THAI BAHT \par \par \uc2  The baht finally caught up with the other Southeast Asian \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and broke the 45 to the dollar mark for the first \par \par \uc2  time since June 8. \par \par \uc2  Bangkok dealers said Singapore-based players kicked off the \par \par \uc2  long dollar unwinding, which triggered stop-loss dollar sell \par \par \uc2  orders around 45.20. \par \par \uc2  They added the baht was mainly inspired by the stronger \par \par \uc2  regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  later gained momentum \par \par \uc2  when the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \par \par \uc2  market. The bank added the baht was stable and in line with \par \par \uc2  regionals. \par \par \uc2  The market had been bracing for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy \par \par \uc2  dollars to maintain export competitiveness, and took those \par \par \uc2  comments to signal the bank's approval of the baht's gains. \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar was quoted around 1.7582 in late \par \par \uc2  trade, marginally up from 1.7584 late on Monday, after choppy \par \par \uc2  trading. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the Sing dollar was mostly tracking the yen. \par \par \uc2  However, dollar appetite has been dulled by the recent spate of \par \par \uc2  long dollar unwinding by funds that burned many players. \par \par \uc2  Charts showed the dollar/Sing languishing in oversold \par \par \uc2  territory with a 14-day relative strength index reading of \par \par \uc2  17.696. It has been oversold since July 24. \par \par \uc2  INDONESIAN RUPIAH \par \par \uc2  The rupiah was anchored within a 8,400-8,500 range after \par \par \uc2  sharply surging to 11-month highs around 8,225 in early trade. \par \par \uc2  Jakarta dealers said the sudden rise was caused by \par \par \uc2  interbank players liquidating their long dollar positions on \par \par \uc2  fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push the rupiah higher. \par \par \uc2  But the market later realised there was no supply of \par \par \uc2  dollars from authorities and local corporates jumped in to buy \par \par \uc2  dollars. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  denied it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week, but \par \par \uc2  dealers believed it sold up to $50 million late on Monday. \par \par \uc2      The rupiah has risen by about 30 percent since President \par \par \uc2  Megawati Sukarnoputri took office on July 23. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  deputy governor Miranda Goeltom said she \par \par \uc2  was not worried by the abrupt surge. But chief economics \par \par \uc2  minister Dorodjatun Kuntjoro-Jakti warned earlier pace of the \par \par \uc2  rise could hurt the economy. \par \par \uc2  The IMF praised the new government's determination to \par \par \uc2  reforms and said a mission would visit Indonesia next week to \par \par \uc2  work out an early resumption of lending. \par \par \uc2  PHILIPPINE PESO \par \par \uc2  The peso edged higher, but was unable to hit Monday's highs \par \par \uc2  around 51 as dollar inflows dwindled. \par \par \uc2      But Manila dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's moves to push \par \par \uc2  the peso higher kept players from taking aggressive positions. \par \par \uc2      The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has raised liquidity requirements by a \par \par \uc2  total of four percentage points to 11 percent in recent weeks, \par \par \uc2  squeezing peso liquidity and last week it penalised nine banks \par \par \uc2  for \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  rule violations. \par \par \uc2  KOREAN WON -2 \par \par \uc2  The won was off its intraday high of 1,286.7 as importers \par \par \uc2  covered short dollar positions ahead of a holiday and foreign \par \par \uc2  investors settled some of their recent sales of local stocks. \par \par \uc2  Players were also cautious not to push the won higher on \par \par \uc2  wariness of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after a state bank bought dollars on \par \par \uc2  Friday when the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit two-month highs. \par \par \uc2      Foreign investors sold a net 201.8 billion won worth of \par \par \uc2  shares in the past three sessions. \par \par \uc2      Even though Korean stocks closed at five-week high on \par \par \uc2  Tuesday, foreign investors were net sellers, offloading another \par \par \uc2  12.6 billion won in shares. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     TAIWAN DOLLAR\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The Taiwan dollar was locked in a tight 34.546-34.578 range\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in a dearth of fresh leads.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     Market participants were cautious ahead of Friday's release\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of second-quarter gross domestic product data.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was underpinned by local stock purchases by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investors who bought a net T$458.8 million (US$13.3\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par million) worth of shares on Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     On the macro front, economists polled by Reuters expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the island's second-quarter current account surplus to triple\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par to US$3.32 billion from a year ago as imports posted a larger\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par year-on-year decline than exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will issue current account data on Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. $0820 GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Change on the day\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid     Prev Close    Pct Move\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Japan yen     122.61       121.80         -0.66\par  Sing dlr      1.7587       1.7584         -0.02\par  Taiwan dlr    34.582       34.599         +0.05\par  Korean won   1287.00      1281.00         -0.47\par  Baht           44.81        45.11         +0.67\par  Peso           51.17        51.21         +0.08\par  Rupiah       8430.00      8520.00         +1.07\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on year\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2       Latest     End prev yr     Pct Move\par  Japan yen     122.61       114.45         -6.66\par  Sing dlr      1.7587       1.7365         -1.26\par  Taiwan dlr    34.582       32.900         -4.86\par  Korean won   1287.00      1277.00         -0.78\par  Baht           44.81        43.70         -2.48\par  Peso           51.17        50.75         -0.82\par  Rupiah       8430.00      9470.00        +12.34\par  Ringgit       3.7995       3.7995         +0.00.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010814dx8e00i2m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
