\par\par \b \uc2  Thai Baht Ends Up On Strength In Other Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 604 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2001\par 13:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BANGKOK -(Dow Jones)- The Thai baht rose against the U.S. dollar in Asian spot trade Tuesday, supported by strength in other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The U.S. dollar finished at 44.965 baht, down from THB45.19 in other Asian markets late Monday, and from THB45.315 at the Bangkok close Friday. \par \par \uc2  Thai markets were closed Monday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  It was the first time since early June that the dollar fell below THB45.00. \par \par \uc2  Dollar-selling on concerns about weakness in the U.S. economy triggered stop-loss selling just above THB45.00 in early trade Tuesday, but local corporate demand and fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept the dollar above support at THB44.80. \par \par \uc2  The dollar moved back above THB45.00 after Bank of Japan announced a surprise easing in its monetary policy, but fell below that level in the afternoon as concerns about the U.S. economy reasserted themselves. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the baht has lagged behind regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in their gains on the dollar recently, but it played catch up Tuesday, moving quickly when leading regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose against the dollar, but barely moving when they retreated. \par \par \uc2  The yen and Singapore dollar should continue to set the tone for the baht, but support for the U.S. dollar should be underpinned by local corporate demand at THB44.80. \par \par \uc2  Stop-loss selling easily overwhelmed local demand Tuesday, but investors haven't been aggressive in building up long-dollar positions against the baht, so there may not be as much stop-loss selling if the dollar approaches its next support levels, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The dollar is expected to open Wednesday in a range of THB44.80 to THB45.05, subject to regional volatility. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Thailand intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the last time the dollar fell to the THB44.70 to THB44.80 range, giving the support level an added psychological boost. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula said Tuesday that the\par authorities haven't been \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervening\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market\par recently, as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has been moving naturally in line with the\par market.\par - - 14/08/01 11-55G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thai government bond yields were mixed in very thin trading Tuesday,\par on continuing uncertainty over the government's intentions toward\par short-term interest rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has said it expects short-term rates to remain stable\par through the rest of the year, but authorities were also arranging to\par soak up excess liquidity with a massive THB320 billion in\par government-guaranteed bonds, to be issued in the fourth quarter by the\par Financial Institutions Development Fund.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai Bond Dealing Center said in its daily report that the yield\par on the government bond due December 2006 closed at 5.865%, down from a\par last deal Friday at 5.90%, while the December 2008 issue was flat at\par 6.23%.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HSBC said in its weekly market report that bonds of six and seven\par years had overshot the yield curve last week, and were due for a\par correction.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Money market interest rates were mostly flat, on flush liquidity. The\par overnight repurchase market rate rose slightly, however, as extra cash\par put into circulation ahead of the long weekend hadn't yet returned to\par financial institutions, the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  said on its Web site.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Market      Term                    Tuesday      Monday\par Interbank  Overnight/Most Active    2.3750%      2.3750%\par Repurchase Overnight/Close          2.3750%      2.1250%\par            14-Day                   2.5000%      2.5000%\par            1-Month                no activity    2.5625%\par            3-Month                  2.7500%      2.7500%\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Tom Fox, Dow Jones Newswires; 662 266 0744; tom.fox@dowjones.com\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1028 1861 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010814dx8e000l3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
