\par\par \b \uc2  Most Asian  \highlight22\uc2 Currencies \highlight\uc2  Higher Late; Rupiah Continues Rally \b0\par\par\uc2  By Alan Yonan Jr. \par \uc2 786 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Juli 2001\par 11:48\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dow Jones Newswires \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE -(Dow Jones)- The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market continued to cheer Megawati Sukarnoputri's rise to the Indonesian presidency as the rupiah rallied to a five month high Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Although Megawati has offered few details about how she plans to turn around Indonesia's struggling economy, analysts said market players were simply hopeful she would do a better job than her predecessor, Abdurrahman Wahid. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah began is surge Monday when it became clear Wahid's departure was imminent. Indonesian lawmakers, who had accused Wahid of corruption and incompetence, followed through with their pledge to remove him from office and by late Monday had named Megawati as his successor. \par \par \uc2  The market euphoria proved contagious, fueling gains in the neighboring Singapore dollar and Thai baht for a second day in a row Tuesday. The South Korean won and New Taiwan dollar also finished stronger, although the Philippine peso was weaker. \par \par \uc2  The rupiah traded as high as 9,750 against the dollar during the Asian day Tuesday, its best performance since February 26 when it strengthened to IDR9,600. Late in the session the dollar was quoted at IDR9,850, down from 10,230 late Monday. \par \par \uc2  The market will now be closely watching to see who Megawati appoints to key cabinet positions, such as finance minister and minister for economics. \par \par \uc2  Near the top of the list of candidates is Lakasamana Sukardi, a well respected and former state enterprises minister who has won accolades for insisting on reform and strengthening of the judicial system. \par \par \uc2  Megawati must not make the mistake of choosing her cabinet based on political considerations, something Wahid was accused of, said Richard Baker, an Indonesia expert at the East-West Center in Honolulu. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This isn't the time for politics as usual," Baker said. He added that\par "Megawati has to be given the ability to pick her people based on the\par basis of competence and to develop a set of policies that realistically\par meet the country's needs."\par - - 24/07/01 09-48G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Singapore dollar was also helped by the improved sentiment toward\par the rupiah, as well as market expectations of an off-budget economic\par stimulus package the government is scheduled to unveil Wednesday,\par dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar was quoted at S$1.8191 in late Asian trading, down\par from S$1.8240 late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par There's a chance the Singapore \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  could strengthen further to\par S$1.8100 to S$1.8150 against the U.S. dollar if the yen were to rise\par unexpectedly, or the rupiah "rallied massively," according to UBS\par Warburg.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "But this isn't our best case. Instead we expect the U.S. dollar to\par remain supported on dips below S$1.8200 and resume its upward grind back\par towards S$1.8500."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Thai baht continued to rebound from a 40-month low touched early\par Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders said they suspected official \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par because institutions that usually act on behalf of the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  were\par active in the market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par But Bank of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Thailand\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Governor Pridiyathorn Devakula denied the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and said he was satisfied with the baht's current\par stability.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Late in Asia the dollar was quoted at 45.170 baht, down from THB45.746\par late Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The New Taiwan dollar finished stronger for the fifth consecutive\par session on continued U.S. dollar-selling by exporters and offshore\par players.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The U.S. dollar closed at NT$34.878, compared with NT$34.893 Monday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Analysts said the New Taiwan dollar's rise is expected to be\par short-lived because it will take more substantive factors, such as signs\par of an economic recovery, to sustain a rise in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The South Korean won edged higher as the local stock market recovered\par some of Monday's losses.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar finished at 1,308.5 won, slightly down from Monday's close\par of KRW1,309.3.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Although foreigners were net sellers of shares, the fact that the\par overall index finished higher provided some relief to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign\par exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The Philippine peso was pressured by lingering domestic economic and\par security concerns along with the weakness in the yen, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar's gains were capped by banks exercising caution on bidding\par up the dollar after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  revealed plans to implement new\par measures to curb \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  speculation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar closed at 53.550 pesos on the Philippine Dealing System, up\par from PHP53.400 Monday. The dollar hit an intraday high of PHP53.600 and\par averaged PHP53.552.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Alan Yonan Jr., Dow Jones Newswires; 65 9862-0905;\par alan.yonan@dowjones.com.\par -0- 24/07/01 10-30G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1136 4250 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010724dx7o000px\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Thailand near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\